1
00:01:09,199 --> 00:01:12,072
Halley: SOMETIMES,
LIFE IS SO PERFECT.

2
00:01:12,202 --> 00:01:13,421
ISN'T IT?

3
00:01:13,551 --> 00:01:15,118
IT HAS TO BE,

4
00:01:15,249 --> 00:01:17,642
TO MAKE UP FOR THE HARD STUFF
IT THROWS YOUR WAY.

5
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:23,735
YOU HAVE TO LEARN TO WALK,

6
00:01:23,866 --> 00:01:25,476
YOU HAVE TO LEARN TO TALK.

7
00:01:27,522 --> 00:01:29,263
YOU HAVE TO WEAR

8
00:01:29,393 --> 00:01:32,788
THAT TOTALLY RIDICULOUS HAT
YOUR GRANDMA BOUGHT YOU.

9
00:01:32,918 --> 00:01:35,921
YOU HAVE
NO SAY IN THE MATTER.

10
00:01:36,052 --> 00:01:37,488
AND WHEN YOU'RE
A LITTLE OLDER,

11
00:01:37,619 --> 00:01:39,229
EVEN THOUGH YOU GET
TO CHOOSE YOUR HATS,

12
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,188
YOU DON'T GET TO CHOOSE
WHAT THEY PUT

13
00:01:41,318 --> 00:01:43,581
IN THOSE MEATBALLS
AT THE CAFETERIA...

14
00:01:43,712 --> 00:01:45,670
OR WHEN TO FALL IN LOVE.

15
00:01:49,674 --> 00:01:53,678
THINGS HAPPEN,
AND YOU JUST HAVE TO DEAL.

16
00:01:58,770 --> 00:02:01,077
Recording: AND BREATHE.

17
00:02:02,948 --> 00:02:04,254
LET'S JUST THINK OF THE DAY

18
00:02:04,385 --> 00:02:05,603
MY PARENT'S DIVORCE
CAME THROUGH

19
00:02:05,734 --> 00:02:09,085
AS "BIG, UGLY HAT DAY."

20
00:02:10,608 --> 00:02:14,090
REFER TO DIAGRAM B
ON PAGE 19--

21
00:02:14,221 --> 00:02:17,267
"THE TREE OF LIFE."

22
00:02:17,398 --> 00:02:19,095
AND BREATHE.

23
00:02:19,226 --> 00:02:23,143
Woman: ...ANYBODY BUT HIS OWN
SELFISH PLEASURE.

24
00:02:23,273 --> 00:02:24,144
Girl: MOM, PLEASE.

25
00:02:24,274 --> 00:02:25,145
Recording: FOCUS.

26
00:02:25,275 --> 00:02:26,320
Woman: I COULDN'T CARE LESS

27
00:02:26,450 --> 00:02:29,192
ABOUT YOUR FATHER'S
MID-LIFE CRISIS

28
00:02:29,323 --> 00:02:32,195
AND COMPLETE MOCKERY
OF HIS WEDDING VOWS.

29
00:02:33,762 --> 00:02:35,503
I JUST HOPE HE DOESN'T
EXPECT ME--

30
00:02:35,633 --> 00:02:38,027
OH, HALLEY, I'M SORRY.
I DIDN'T SEE YOU THERE.

31
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,071
GUYS...

32
00:02:39,202 --> 00:02:40,595
WHERE DO YOU THINK
YOU'RE GOING?

33
00:02:40,725 --> 00:02:42,771
AS LONG AS YOU'RE GONNA
KILL ME WITH FLYING ICE,

34
00:02:42,901 --> 00:02:43,815
DOES IT REALLY MATTER?

35
00:02:43,946 --> 00:02:44,990
EXCUSE ME, EVERYONE.

36
00:02:45,121 --> 00:02:46,601
HALLEY!MOM!

37
00:02:46,731 --> 00:02:49,386
I HAVE SOME REALLY
IMPORTANT NEWS TO ANNOUNCE HERE.

38
00:02:49,517 --> 00:02:52,520
LEWIS AND I--
WE'RE GETTING MARRIED.

39
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:54,870
HE ASKED ME
LAST SATURDAY NIGHT.

40
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,134
I WANTED TO TELL YOU,
BUT I WASN'T SURE WHEN,

41
00:02:58,265 --> 00:02:59,657
OR HOW YOU'D REACT.

42
00:02:59,788 --> 00:03:01,920
I TOLD HIM I COULDN'T
EVEN WEAR THIS RING

43
00:03:02,051 --> 00:03:03,922
UNTIL AFTER I TALKED
TO YOU.

44
00:03:04,053 --> 00:03:06,490
BUT WE WANNA HAVE
THIS BIG SPRING WEDDING,

45
00:03:06,621 --> 00:03:08,275
MOM, I'M SO HAPPY.

46
00:03:18,633 --> 00:03:19,808
NICE TIMING, HUH?

47
00:03:21,418 --> 00:03:22,767
TELL YOUR MOM
YOU'RE GETTING MARRIED

48
00:03:22,898 --> 00:03:25,030
ON THE DAY
SHE GETS DIVORCED.

49
00:03:25,161 --> 00:03:27,642
WHY DOES LOVE
MAKE PEOPLE CRAZY?

50
00:03:30,819 --> 00:03:33,996
Girl: OH! OH, MY--

51
00:03:34,126 --> 00:03:35,171
OH!

52
00:03:38,827 --> 00:03:41,046
OH, SCARLETT, YOU WEREN'T
PICKING UP YOUR PHONE.

53
00:03:41,177 --> 00:03:42,483
I'M SO SORRY!

54
00:03:42,613 --> 00:03:43,658
[ laughs ]

55
00:03:43,788 --> 00:03:47,314
UM...OH, UH, HALLEY,
THAT'S MICHAEL.

56
00:03:47,444 --> 00:03:48,445
MICHAEL, UH...

57
00:03:48,576 --> 00:03:50,012
HI.

58
00:03:50,142 --> 00:03:51,274
MM-HM.

59
00:03:52,362 --> 00:03:53,494
Michael: THANK YOU.

60
00:03:55,322 --> 00:03:56,845
[ motorcycle revs ]

61
00:03:58,107 --> 00:04:00,588
BYE! I LOVE YOU!

62
00:04:02,416 --> 00:04:03,460
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

63
00:04:05,549 --> 00:04:06,681
WOW.

64
00:04:06,811 --> 00:04:09,684
YOU, UM, DIDN'T TELL ME
YOU WERE DOING IT.

65
00:04:09,814 --> 00:04:10,859
OH...

66
00:04:11,947 --> 00:04:14,123
WHEN YOU MEET
THE RIGHT PERSON

67
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:15,907
AND YOU FALL IN LOVE...

68
00:04:18,388 --> 00:04:22,000
IT'S LIKE...IT'S LIKE
EVERYTHING YOU THOUGHT,

69
00:04:22,131 --> 00:04:24,916
YOU THOUGHT IS...OH!

70
00:04:25,047 --> 00:04:26,222
CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

71
00:04:26,353 --> 00:04:28,180
NO. I CAN'T.

72
00:04:28,311 --> 00:04:30,226
SCARLETT, COME ON.

73
00:04:30,357 --> 00:04:32,272
YOU ARE SOUNDING
DANGEROUSLY CLOSE

74
00:04:32,402 --> 00:04:34,883
TO A HALLMARK
GREETING CARD.

75
00:04:35,013 --> 00:04:36,798
YOU'RE GONNA LET YOURSELF
TURN INTO MUSH

76
00:04:36,928 --> 00:04:39,496
OVER SOMETHING LIKE SEX?

77
00:04:39,627 --> 00:04:42,456
UM...YEAH.

78
00:04:42,586 --> 00:04:44,980
YOU CAN'T EXPECT TO DO
ANYTHING GREAT IN LIFE

79
00:04:45,110 --> 00:04:48,766
IF YOU BUCKLE THE FIRST TIME
SOME GUY BATS HIS EYES AT YOU.

80
00:04:48,897 --> 00:04:50,464
NEWS FLASH, HAL--

81
00:04:50,594 --> 00:04:54,119
EVEN MADONNA
EVENTUALLY GOT MARRIED.

82
00:04:54,250 --> 00:04:57,906
MY MOM THINKS THAT MEANS
THERE'S HOPE FOR HER, TOO.

83
00:05:00,648 --> 00:05:03,694
YOUR MOM WANTS
TO GET MARRIED?

84
00:05:03,825 --> 00:05:06,088
WELL, SHE WANTS TO FALL
IN LOVE, HALLEY.

85
00:05:07,742 --> 00:05:08,917
EVERYONE DOES.

86
00:05:09,047 --> 00:05:12,877
HI. I'VE BEEN IN--

87
00:05:13,008 --> 00:05:15,663
HI. I'VE BEEN DIVORCED
FOR A LONG TIME,

88
00:05:15,793 --> 00:05:19,231
SO MY BAGGAGE
IS ANCIENT HISTORY.

89
00:05:19,362 --> 00:05:22,844
I LIKE TO THINK THAT I
TRAVEL LIGHT THESE DAYS.

90
00:05:22,974 --> 00:05:24,367
EXCEPT FOR
MY DAUGHTER SCARLETT,

91
00:05:24,498 --> 00:05:27,501
WHO IS JUST A JOY
OF A CARRYON.

92
00:05:29,416 --> 00:05:32,027
SEE, I THINK I'M TAKING
THE BAGGAGE THING TOO FAR.

93
00:05:34,943 --> 00:05:36,161
MAYBE I SHOULD START OVER.

94
00:05:36,292 --> 00:05:38,338
YOU KNOW WHAT I THINK
OF THIS WHOLE IDEA.

95
00:05:38,468 --> 00:05:40,731
I'M ONLY GONNA SEND IT
TO THE ONLINE GUYS

96
00:05:40,862 --> 00:05:45,649
WHO PASS MY RIGID
FIVE-POINT CHECKLIST.

97
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:46,650
HERE, YOU TRY.

98
00:05:46,781 --> 00:05:48,522
GO AWAY.

99
00:05:48,652 --> 00:05:52,352
LYDIA, THE MAN OF YOUR DREAMS
IS SITTING OUT THERE RIGHT NOW

100
00:05:52,482 --> 00:05:54,963
WAITING TO HEAR FROM YOU.
SPEAK TO HIM.

101
00:05:55,093 --> 00:05:56,399
I DON'T THINK
THE PERFECT MAN

102
00:05:56,530 --> 00:05:58,749
IS GONNA WANT TO HEAR
WHAT I HAVE TO SAY.

103
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:01,012
SURE HE DOES, SWEETIE.
SPEAK TO HIM.

104
00:06:02,013 --> 00:06:03,188
GO ON.

105
00:06:07,149 --> 00:06:08,759
I'M SORRY, MR. PERFECT,

106
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:10,718
BUT IF YOU'RE WAITING FOR ME,

107
00:06:10,848 --> 00:06:12,981
IT'S GONNA BE
A HELL OF A LONG WAIT.

108
00:06:13,111 --> 00:06:16,898
SEE, I'VE HAD IT
WITH MEN LIKE YOU.

109
00:06:17,028 --> 00:06:20,380
MM-HM. I THINK IT'S TERRIFIC
THAT YOU HAVE A GREAT JOB,

110
00:06:20,510 --> 00:06:23,121
AND YOU'RE SENSITIVE
TO THE NEEDS OF OTHERS,

111
00:06:23,252 --> 00:06:28,431
AND YOU JOG THREE TIMES A WEEK
TO KEEP THE BELLY AT BAY,

112
00:06:28,562 --> 00:06:30,520
BUT THE SECOND
SOME SILICON-BREASTED,

113
00:06:30,651 --> 00:06:33,610
BUTT-KISSING, AIRHEAD CLIMBER
HALF YOUR AGE COMES ALONG,

114
00:06:33,741 --> 00:06:35,569
YOU CAN'T KEEP
YOUR PANTS ZIPPED.

115
00:06:35,699 --> 00:06:36,744
WELL, FUCK YOU!

116
00:06:36,874 --> 00:06:38,572
THAT'S RIGHT, MR. MIDDLE-AGE,

117
00:06:38,702 --> 00:06:41,052
THINK-YOU'RE-A-BIG-SHOT,
PHONY ASSHOLE.

118
00:06:41,183 --> 00:06:43,446
YOU AIN'T GETTIN' ANY FROM ME.

119
00:06:45,883 --> 00:06:47,450
OKAY.

120
00:06:47,581 --> 00:06:50,410
I THINK WE'LL JUST
GIVE THIS A LITTLE TIME.

121
00:06:53,935 --> 00:06:57,329
[ imitates leaky faucet ]

122
00:06:57,460 --> 00:06:59,767
[ mutters ]
So juvenile.

123
00:07:05,076 --> 00:07:06,991
I'M GLAD YOU'RE
BACK EARLY FROM CAMP.

124
00:07:07,122 --> 00:07:08,819
EVEN THOUGH IT WAS
A DISHONORABLE DISCHARGE.

125
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:10,255
WHAT HAPPENED?

126
00:07:10,386 --> 00:07:12,562
WHERE WERE YOU TRYING TO GET TO
IN THAT OLD CANOE?

127
00:07:12,693 --> 00:07:13,694
NO COMMENT.

128
00:07:13,824 --> 00:07:15,435
NO COMMENT?

129
00:07:15,565 --> 00:07:17,698
I DON'T SPEAK TO THE PRESS.

130
00:07:17,828 --> 00:07:19,221
I'M THE PRESS?

131
00:07:19,351 --> 00:07:22,833
YEAH, AND ANYTHING I SAY CAN
AND WILL BE USED AGAINST ME.

132
00:07:22,964 --> 00:07:24,618
I WOULD NEVER USE
ANYTHING AGAINST YOU.

133
00:07:24,748 --> 00:07:27,185
OH, DAD, GIVE IT UP!
IT'S OLD.

134
00:07:27,316 --> 00:07:29,274
AND YOU NEED TO GET
YOUR OWN MATERIAL.

135
00:07:29,405 --> 00:07:30,319
Man: DADDY DOG.

136
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:31,276
YO.

137
00:07:31,407 --> 00:07:33,017
LEN MARTIN.
IT'S YOU, RIGHT?

138
00:07:33,148 --> 00:07:35,846
WDYG'S COOLEST DEEJAY.

139
00:07:35,977 --> 00:07:37,500
THAT'S ME.

140
00:07:37,631 --> 00:07:38,936
"WE DIG THE DOG!"

141
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:40,024
[ makes barking sound ]

142
00:07:40,155 --> 00:07:41,025
LOVE YOUR SHOW, MAN.

143
00:07:41,156 --> 00:07:42,157
THANKS, MAN.

144
00:07:43,419 --> 00:07:46,727
YOU ARE THE HIPPEST
OLD GUY I KNOW.

145
00:07:46,857 --> 00:07:48,032
YO, DUDE!

146
00:07:48,163 --> 00:07:49,686
I'M NOT THAT OLD!

147
00:07:51,166 --> 00:07:53,560
[ howling noise ]

148
00:07:53,690 --> 00:07:55,518
[ howling noise ]

149
00:07:55,649 --> 00:07:57,477
THAT'S LEN MARTIN.

150
00:07:57,607 --> 00:07:58,956
[ barks ]HEY!

151
00:08:02,090 --> 00:08:04,005
Woman: HELLO, GORGEOUS ONES.

152
00:08:04,135 --> 00:08:06,224
AND YOU INVITED HER.

153
00:08:06,355 --> 00:08:07,878
HEY, BABY.

154
00:08:08,009 --> 00:08:09,227
HEY.

155
00:08:09,358 --> 00:08:10,707
I THOUGHT WE'D SPEND
SOME TIME TOGETHER,

156
00:08:10,838 --> 00:08:12,666
THEN WE COULD HAVE
A CHANCE TO BOND.

157
00:08:16,713 --> 00:08:20,630
WELL...LOOK AT YOU, HALLEY.

158
00:08:20,761 --> 00:08:23,503
THAT'S HARD TO DO
WITHOUT A MIRROR, ISN'T IT?

159
00:08:25,113 --> 00:08:27,768
HONEY, YOU KEEP
GETTING PRETTIER EVERY DAY.

160
00:08:27,898 --> 00:08:29,987
I HAVE NO IDEA HOW YOU
COULD SAY THAT

161
00:08:30,118 --> 00:08:33,600
'CAUSE YOU DEFINITELY
DON'T SEE ME EVERY DAY.

162
00:08:33,730 --> 00:08:36,428
AND YESTERDAY,
OH, MY GOD, I WAS SO UGLY.

163
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,474
AND LAST WEDNESDAY,
THAT SUCKED, TOO.

164
00:08:38,605 --> 00:08:41,651
SO IT'S KIND OF
A DAY TO DAY THING.

165
00:08:43,479 --> 00:08:45,002
I LOVE THAT SENSE OF HUMOR.

166
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:49,529
JUST LIKE HER DADDY.

167
00:08:51,269 --> 00:08:52,532
LOOK AT THAT GORGEOUS GIRL.

168
00:08:52,662 --> 00:08:53,750
DAD, STOP IT.

169
00:08:53,881 --> 00:08:56,013
SHE'S GOT
HER DADDY'S HAIR.

170
00:08:56,144 --> 00:08:57,101
DON'T CUT IT.

171
00:08:57,232 --> 00:08:58,320
IT'S BEAUTIFUL.

172
00:08:58,450 --> 00:09:00,627
DON'T CUT IT.
JUST LET IT GROW.

173
00:09:00,757 --> 00:09:01,976
DON'T CUT IT.

174
00:09:02,106 --> 00:09:03,760
CUT IT.

175
00:09:03,891 --> 00:09:05,022
OKAY.

176
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:12,682
LET ME COUNT THE WAYS
THAT THIS CARD CAN BE USED

177
00:09:12,813 --> 00:09:13,988
TO INDUCE...

178
00:09:14,118 --> 00:09:17,905
NAUSEA,
GASTRIC DISTRESS, VOMITING.

179
00:09:18,035 --> 00:09:20,429
YEAH, GO AHEAD AND MOCK ME,
BUT THIS IS SERIOUS.

180
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,432
I NEED TO FIND SOMETHING FUNNY
AND SOMETHING SWEET,

181
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:24,607
JUST THE WAY SCARLETT IS.

182
00:09:24,738 --> 00:09:26,087
REMEMBER LAST TIME
I GOT HER--

183
00:09:26,217 --> 00:09:28,132
OKAY. OKAY.
WELL, LOOK, HERE'S ONE.

184
00:09:28,263 --> 00:09:29,394
NOT HELPING.

185
00:09:29,525 --> 00:09:31,875
"FROM SMALL BEGINNINGS
COME GREAT THINGS."

186
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:36,750
"CONGRATULATIONS
ON YOUR NEW BABY."

187
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,447
I THOUGHT YOU WERE
GONNA HELP ME.

188
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:39,970
LIGHTEN UP, SHERWOOD.

189
00:09:40,101 --> 00:09:43,234
"THE FIRST TIME WE MET,
YOU STOLE MY HEART."

190
00:09:45,802 --> 00:09:47,935
"GOOD LUCK IN FINDING
A COMPATIBLE ORGAN DONOR."

191
00:09:48,065 --> 00:09:49,110
NICE!

192
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:51,852
I'M KIDDING, OKAY?
IT'S BLANK INSIDE.

193
00:09:51,982 --> 00:09:54,811
YOU KNOW SOMETHING?
YOU'RE NOT FUNNY, FORRESTER.

194
00:09:54,942 --> 00:09:57,292
THIS GIRL IS AMAZING--
UNLIKE YOU.

195
00:09:57,422 --> 00:10:00,164
AND SHE'S SENSITIVE--
UNLIKE YOU.

196
00:10:00,295 --> 00:10:01,818
AND SHE'S SEXY.

197
00:10:01,949 --> 00:10:03,341
UNLIKE YOU.UNLIKE ME.

198
00:10:03,472 --> 00:10:05,169
Forrester: THERE'S GOTTA
BE A CARD HERE

199
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:08,608
FOR A REDHEAD
FROM A NEWLY SMITTEN

200
00:10:08,738 --> 00:10:10,740
HUNKA-HUNKA
BURNIN' LOVE.

201
00:10:10,871 --> 00:10:13,395
I MEAN...LOOK.

202
00:10:13,525 --> 00:10:15,745
SUMMER ROMANCE
HAS ITS OWN SECTION.

203
00:10:16,790 --> 00:10:19,183
IT'S NOT A SUMMER ROMANCE.
I MEAN...

204
00:10:19,314 --> 00:10:20,358
SCARLETT IS...

205
00:10:20,489 --> 00:10:22,970
STANDING
RIGHT BEHIND YOU...DUDE.

206
00:10:25,712 --> 00:10:26,713
HI.

207
00:10:30,238 --> 00:10:31,543
Michael: SNEAKING UP ON ME?

208
00:10:31,674 --> 00:10:32,980
[ clears throat ]

209
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:34,024
HI, HALLEY.

210
00:10:34,155 --> 00:10:36,636
HI.

211
00:10:36,766 --> 00:10:38,855
[ giggling ]

212
00:10:38,986 --> 00:10:40,901
YOU REMEMBER MY NAME?

213
00:10:41,031 --> 00:10:42,859
SURE. WE WERE
IN BIOLOGY TOGETHER.

214
00:10:42,990 --> 00:10:45,383
YEAH, I KNOW, BUT...

215
00:10:45,514 --> 00:10:48,125
YOU WERE NEVER THERE.
REALLY. TECHNICALLY.

216
00:10:49,866 --> 00:10:51,520
I LIKE YOUR HAIR.

217
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:53,000
THANK YOU.

218
00:10:54,871 --> 00:10:57,831
♪ I DON'T NEED
TO READ BILLY SHAKESPEARE ♪

219
00:10:57,961 --> 00:11:01,791
♪ MEET JULIET
OR MY VOLIO ♪

220
00:11:01,922 --> 00:11:05,316
♪ FEEL FOR ONCE
WHAT IT'S LIKE TO REBEL NOW ♪

221
00:11:05,447 --> 00:11:09,103
♪ I WANNA BREAK OUT,
LET'S GO ♪

222
00:11:09,233 --> 00:11:12,541
♪ GET OUT, GET OUT,
GET OUT, GET OUT ♪

223
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:15,587
SEE, MY SCHEDULE IS ALL WRONG,
WHICH, I THINK, IS A SIGN

224
00:11:15,718 --> 00:11:17,938
THAT NOTHING'S GOING
ACCORDING TO PLAN THIS YEAR.

225
00:11:18,068 --> 00:11:21,942
UM, IT'S A COMPLETE
AND TOTAL MESS.

226
00:11:22,072 --> 00:11:24,814
LOOKS LIKE A FINE SCHEDULE
TO ME, HALLEY.

227
00:11:24,945 --> 00:11:27,034
NO. UM, BAND?

228
00:11:27,164 --> 00:11:29,210
I WOULD NEVER
SIGN UP FOR BAND.

229
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:30,515
WHAT'S WRONG WITH BAND?

230
00:11:30,646 --> 00:11:32,126
I DON'T PLAY ANYTHING?

231
00:11:32,256 --> 00:11:35,695
WELL, MAYBE YOU SHOULD.
I'M SURE YOU COULD HANDLE IT.

232
00:11:35,825 --> 00:11:38,219
OKAY, MRS. TOUSSAINT,
THIS IS NOT MY SCHEDULE.

233
00:11:38,349 --> 00:11:39,786
LOOK, I'M SIGNED UP
FOR ALGEBRA,

234
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:41,831
AND I'VE ALREADY
TAKEN CALCULUS.

235
00:11:41,962 --> 00:11:44,268
WELL, MAYBE A BRUSH-UP
IS A GOOD THING,

236
00:11:44,399 --> 00:11:46,096
NOT TO MENTION
A GOOD GRADE.

237
00:11:46,227 --> 00:11:49,404
WHY DON'T YOU GIVE IT A SHOT
BEFORE YOU DECIDE ANYTHING.

238
00:11:49,534 --> 00:11:52,624
OKAY, I'M SIGNED UP
FOR BOYS' P.E.

239
00:11:52,755 --> 00:11:53,843
Radio: 94 FM...

240
00:11:53,974 --> 00:11:57,586
FILL OUT THIS FORM
AND WE'LL START AGAIN.

241
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,501
LEN MARTIN
WITH A TRAFFIC UPDATE

242
00:11:59,631 --> 00:12:01,851
FROM THAT LOVE PUPPY
IN THE SKIES,

243
00:12:01,982 --> 00:12:04,332
OUR VERY OWN LORNA QUEEN.

244
00:12:04,462 --> 00:12:06,116
LORNA, YOU UP THERE?

245
00:12:06,247 --> 00:12:07,639
Lorna: HI, LEN.

246
00:12:07,770 --> 00:12:10,294
ON A CLEAR DAY,
YOU CAN SEE FOREVER.

247
00:12:10,425 --> 00:12:13,515
AND THIS IS
ONE BEAUTIFUL MORNING.

248
00:12:13,645 --> 00:12:15,691
SHOULD WE TELL EVERYONE
OUR LITTLE SECRET?

249
00:12:15,822 --> 00:12:19,129
Len: CAREFUL, BABY,
YOU SURE THIS IS THE TIME?

250
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,305
Lorna: I AM BURSTING
AT THE SEAMS

251
00:12:21,436 --> 00:12:23,917
TO TELL EVERYONE
WE'RE ELOPING.

252
00:12:24,047 --> 00:12:25,483
[ Len howls ]

253
00:12:25,614 --> 00:12:27,921
Lorna: OOPS,
I JUST SPILLED THE BEANS.

254
00:12:28,051 --> 00:12:29,400
[ turns radio off ]

255
00:12:34,188 --> 00:12:36,320
HALLEY, THAT IS
YOUR FATHER'S SHOW, RIGHT?

256
00:12:36,451 --> 00:12:37,757
I JUST LOVE IT.

257
00:12:39,933 --> 00:12:40,890
HI.

258
00:12:42,587 --> 00:12:45,329
TELL HIM CONGRATULATIONS.

259
00:12:46,853 --> 00:12:49,377
I'M SURE VERY YOU'RE EXCITED
ABOUT THE UPCOMING NUPTIALS.

260
00:12:52,032 --> 00:12:54,817
MY FATHER AND MY SISTER.

261
00:12:54,948 --> 00:12:56,863
MY SISTER AND MY FATHER?

262
00:12:56,993 --> 00:12:59,822
YOUR FATHER AND YOUR SISTER
ARE GETTING MARRIED?

263
00:12:59,953 --> 00:13:01,432
YEAH.

264
00:13:01,563 --> 00:13:04,392
NO, NOT TO EACH OTHER.

265
00:13:04,522 --> 00:13:05,523
I...

266
00:13:07,438 --> 00:13:10,354
I HAVE TO CHECK SOMETHING
BEFORE I FILL THIS OUT.

267
00:13:13,009 --> 00:13:16,360
SIT DOWN, FORRESTER.

268
00:13:16,491 --> 00:13:19,581
LET'S SEE IF WE CAN SORT OUT
YOUR USUAL CHAOS.

269
00:13:19,711 --> 00:13:21,061
MAYBE YOU'LL EVEN DO US

270
00:13:21,191 --> 00:13:22,671
THE HONOR OF ATTENDING
THIS YEAR.

271
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:23,977
OKAY, LATER, M.T.

272
00:13:24,107 --> 00:13:25,369
I GOTTA RETHINK
THAT SHOP CLASS.

273
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:27,328
I'M PRETTY SCARY WITH TOOLS.

274
00:13:30,722 --> 00:13:32,376
OH, MY.

275
00:13:32,507 --> 00:13:34,901
YOU DIDN'T KNOW, DID YOU,
ABOUT YOUR DAD GETTING MARRIED?

276
00:13:35,031 --> 00:13:36,250
YES, I DID.

277
00:13:36,380 --> 00:13:37,817
THE BASTARD.

278
00:13:37,947 --> 00:13:39,819
HE TELLS THE WHOLE WORLD
BEFORE HE TELLS YOU.

279
00:13:39,949 --> 00:13:41,081
HE'S NOT...

280
00:13:42,952 --> 00:13:43,910
WHATEVER.

281
00:13:45,694 --> 00:13:46,913
AT LEAST IF THEY'RE ELOPING,

282
00:13:47,043 --> 00:13:48,915
YOU WON'T HAVE TO GO
TO THE WEDDING.

283
00:13:49,045 --> 00:13:51,787
I MEAN, COME ON,
WEDDINGS ARE THE WORST.

284
00:13:51,918 --> 00:13:55,573
ME? I'VE HAD TO GO TO, LIKE,
FIVE BETWEEN MY PARENTS.

285
00:13:55,704 --> 00:13:57,053
DON'T ASK.

286
00:14:00,013 --> 00:14:03,538
LISTEN, M.T. WASN'T GIVING YOU
A HARD TIME BACK THERE, WAS SHE?

287
00:14:03,668 --> 00:14:05,366
"M.T."?

288
00:14:05,496 --> 00:14:08,978
MRS. TOUSSAINT AND I...
WE'RE ON CLOSE TERMS.

289
00:14:09,109 --> 00:14:11,807
YOU GET TO KNOW YOUR
GUIDANCE COUNSELOR REALLY WELL

290
00:14:11,938 --> 00:14:15,202
WHEN YOU'RE CLEARLY
IN DESPERATE NEED OF GUIDANCE.

291
00:14:15,332 --> 00:14:18,074
SEE, I'VE GOT IT
DOWN TO A SCIENCE.

292
00:14:18,205 --> 00:14:19,946
YOU TRY THE JEDI MIND TRICK.

293
00:14:22,165 --> 00:14:23,210
WHAT'S THAT?

294
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:24,428
YOU NEVER SAW
STAR WARS?

295
00:14:24,559 --> 00:14:26,126
NO, I SAW IT.

296
00:14:26,256 --> 00:14:28,650
I GUESS I JUST DIDN'T
MEMORIZE IT LIKE YOU DID.

297
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:30,347
WELL, THAT'S YOUR LOSS,
ISN'T IT?

298
00:14:30,478 --> 00:14:31,740
BECAUSE THE JEDI MIND TRICK

299
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,829
IS WHEN YOU TELL SOMEONE
WHAT TO THINK,

300
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,091
AND THEY THINK IT.

301
00:14:35,222 --> 00:14:37,311
FOR EXAMPLE, M.T. SAYS,

302
00:14:37,441 --> 00:14:39,487
[ nasal voice ] "MACON,
YOU'RE ALREADY IN TROUBLE,

303
00:14:39,617 --> 00:14:41,358
"AND IT'S THE FIRST DAY
OF SCHOOL.

304
00:14:41,489 --> 00:14:44,100
IS THIS ANY WAY
TO START THE NEW YEAR?"

305
00:14:44,231 --> 00:14:46,450
OKAY, PRETEND YOU'RE ME.
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

306
00:14:46,581 --> 00:14:48,888
OKAY. I SAY...

307
00:14:50,411 --> 00:14:53,153
NO. I WANNA BE SOMEONE ELSE.

308
00:14:53,283 --> 00:14:54,154
CUTE. NO.

309
00:14:54,284 --> 00:14:58,636
YOU, AS ME, SAY...

310
00:14:58,767 --> 00:15:02,771
"MRS. T, YOU'RE GONNA
LET THIS ONE SLIDE.

311
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:04,816
BECAUSE IT WAS
AN HONEST MISTAKE,

312
00:15:04,947 --> 00:15:07,515
IT'S ONLY
THE FIRST DAY OF SCHOOL,

313
00:15:07,645 --> 00:15:11,693
AND THE FIRE WAS PUT OUT
AS QUICKLY AS IT WAS STARTED.

314
00:15:11,823 --> 00:15:14,130
YOU DIDN'T REALLY
START A FIRE, DID YOU?

315
00:15:16,567 --> 00:15:19,309
THE POINT IS THAT YOU PUT
THE WORDS INTO SOMEBODY'S MOUTH

316
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,137
AND THEY GIVE THEM
BACK TO YOU

317
00:15:21,268 --> 00:15:23,139
LIKE THEY'VE JUST COME UP
WITH THE IDEA.

318
00:15:23,270 --> 00:15:25,750
LIKE WHEN I ASK YOU TO GO
OUT THIS FRIDAY NIGHT,

319
00:15:25,881 --> 00:15:27,927
YOU'RE GONNA THINK YOU'RE
ASKING ME BECAUSE YOU'LL SAY,

320
00:15:28,057 --> 00:15:29,754
"YES, MACON, I WOULD LOVE TO,

321
00:15:29,885 --> 00:15:31,974
"BECAUSE I KNOW WE'LL HAVE
A TOTALLY GREAT TIME TOGETHER.

322
00:15:32,105 --> 00:15:35,630
IN FACT, I'VE BEEN HOPING
YOU'D ASK ME ALL WEEK."

323
00:15:37,327 --> 00:15:39,373
YOU WANNA GO OUT
ON A DATE WITH ME?

324
00:15:39,503 --> 00:15:42,376
SEE? I TOLD YOU
YOU'D ASK ME.

325
00:15:42,506 --> 00:15:44,639
MACON, I THINK I LIKE YOU
TOO MUCH ALREADY

326
00:15:44,769 --> 00:15:46,597
TO ACTUALLY GO OUT WITH YOU.

327
00:15:48,077 --> 00:15:50,775
WHAT KIND
OF LOGIC IS THAT?

328
00:15:52,516 --> 00:15:54,954
IT'S LOGICAL LOGIC.

329
00:15:55,084 --> 00:15:57,304
THE QUICKEST WAY TO RUIN
A RELATIONSHIP WITH SOMEONE

330
00:15:57,434 --> 00:16:00,307
IS TO ACTUALLY TRY AND HAVE
A RELATIONSHIP WITH THEM.

331
00:16:00,437 --> 00:16:03,049
HAVEN'T YOU NOTICED WHEN
THE OPPOSITE SEX GETS TOGETHER,

332
00:16:03,179 --> 00:16:05,529
EVENTUALLY, SOMEONE
ENDS UP GETTING HURT?

333
00:16:07,662 --> 00:16:10,186
WELL, I AM, TOO--
BOYCOTTING.

334
00:16:10,317 --> 00:16:12,580
YOU CAN'T BOYCOTT
YOUR FATHER'S WEDDING.

335
00:16:12,710 --> 00:16:14,234
IT'S NOT EVEN A WEDDING.

336
00:16:14,364 --> 00:16:16,366
IT'S...AN ELOPEMENT.

337
00:16:16,497 --> 00:16:20,196
YEAH, EXCEPT EVERYONE WITHIN
HIS RADIO FREQUENCY IS INVITED.

338
00:16:20,327 --> 00:16:22,198
MY GOD, HE IS
SUCH A HYPOCRITE.

339
00:16:22,329 --> 00:16:24,722
I CANNOT BELIEVE HE WOULDN'T
TELL US ABOUT IT FIRST.

340
00:16:24,853 --> 00:16:27,943
HE DIDN'T GIVE YOU ANY WARNING
WHEN YOU WENT TO DINNER?

341
00:16:28,074 --> 00:16:29,423
SHE WAS AT THAT DINNER?

342
00:16:29,553 --> 00:16:30,990
NO.

343
00:16:33,644 --> 00:16:36,125
OKAY, YEAH,
SHE WAS THERE AT THE END.

344
00:16:36,256 --> 00:16:39,346
MOM, COME ON. SHE WASN'T
EVEN SUPPOSED TO BE THERE.

345
00:16:39,476 --> 00:16:41,130
YOU KNOW...

346
00:16:41,261 --> 00:16:43,698
I DON'T THINK I'M GONNA LET HIM
WALK ME DOWN THE AISLE.

347
00:16:43,828 --> 00:16:45,178
PLEASE STOP WORRYING
ABOUT ME.

348
00:16:45,308 --> 00:16:46,875
I AM FINE.
I'M FINE.

349
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:50,922
IN A WAY, IT SETS ME FREE.
I FEEL STRANGELY LIBERATED.

350
00:16:51,053 --> 00:16:52,794
AND HE IS
STILL YOUR FATHER, AFTER ALL.

351
00:16:52,924 --> 00:16:54,317
AND IF HE WANTS TO MAKE

352
00:16:54,448 --> 00:16:56,972
A COMPLETE
AND UTTER FOOL OF HIMSELF

353
00:16:57,103 --> 00:17:01,237
BY TRYING IN SOME PATHETICALLY
CLICHé FASHION

354
00:17:01,368 --> 00:17:04,545
TO RECAPTURE
HIS SORRY STATE OF MANHOOD

355
00:17:04,675 --> 00:17:07,635
BY HOOKING UP WITH NOT EVEN
A VERY ATTRACTIVE BIMBO,

356
00:17:07,765 --> 00:17:11,030
THEN IF THAT'S WHAT HE WANTS,
I'M FINE WITH THAT.

357
00:17:12,335 --> 00:17:13,467
SOMEONE TOSS, PLEASE.

358
00:17:16,122 --> 00:17:17,297
NOW.

359
00:17:19,951 --> 00:17:22,084
THIS IS OUR RECEPTION AREA

360
00:17:22,215 --> 00:17:26,567
WITH OUR POST-CEREMONY
CHAMPAGNE BAR...

361
00:17:26,697 --> 00:17:29,048
WHICH IS CONVENIENTLY LOCATED

362
00:17:29,178 --> 00:17:31,528
RIGHT NEXT
TO OUR VERY OWN CHAPEL.

363
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,143
CAN'T YOU JUST PICTURE
WALKING DOWN THIS AISLE?

364
00:17:37,273 --> 00:17:39,623
IN A COFFIN.

365
00:17:39,754 --> 00:17:42,539
SORRY, IT'S JUST...
A LITTLE DEPRESSING.

366
00:17:42,670 --> 00:17:44,976
ACTUALLY, NOBODY'S EVER
SAID THAT BEFORE.

367
00:17:45,107 --> 00:17:48,110
Ashley: LEWIS...SAY SOMETHING.
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

368
00:17:48,241 --> 00:17:51,418
WELL, I LIKE IT.
I MEAN, IT'S VERY CLEAN.

369
00:17:51,548 --> 00:17:53,028
CLEAN?

370
00:17:53,159 --> 00:17:55,422
IS THAT WHAT YOU WANT
OUR WEDDING DAY TO BE?

371
00:17:55,552 --> 00:17:56,684
CLEAN?

372
00:17:56,814 --> 00:17:58,642
IT'S NOT...
IT'S NOT PRETTY,

373
00:17:58,773 --> 00:18:01,297
IT'S NOT INTIMATE,
IT'S NOT ROMANTIC.

374
00:18:01,428 --> 00:18:03,995
I'M JUST SO HAPPY
THAT I GET TO MARRY YOU.

375
00:18:04,126 --> 00:18:05,954
Woman: I'M SORRY,
NOT TO PRESSURE YOU,

376
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:08,304
BUT THIS SPACE DOES BOOK UP
QUITE QUICKLY FOR SPRING.

377
00:18:08,435 --> 00:18:09,827
IN FACT,
WE HAVE ANOTHER COUPLE--

378
00:18:09,958 --> 00:18:12,003
WHY DON'T WE GIVE THEM
A MOMENT TO THINK?

379
00:18:12,134 --> 00:18:16,225
ASHLEY, SWEETIE,
THEY PLAN THE WHOLE THING.

380
00:18:16,356 --> 00:18:20,229
THE FOOD AND THE FLOWERS...
EVEN THE PLACE CARDS.

381
00:18:22,318 --> 00:18:24,755
THINK ABOUT HOW MUCH LESS
HASSLE IT'LL BE.

382
00:18:26,322 --> 00:18:28,455
YOU THINK PLANNING THE MOST
IMPORTANT DAY OF OUR LIVES

383
00:18:28,585 --> 00:18:30,370
IS A HASSLE?

384
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,024
IT HASN'T EVEN
BEEN THAT LONG.

385
00:18:33,155 --> 00:18:34,678
19 1/2 HOURS.

386
00:18:34,809 --> 00:18:35,897
[ gasps ]

387
00:18:36,027 --> 00:18:38,595
WOULDN'T MICHAEL
LOOK COOL IN THAT?

388
00:18:40,206 --> 00:18:42,947
HEY, I DID
A GOOD JOB, HUH?

389
00:18:43,078 --> 00:18:45,515
MICHAEL SHERWOOD WOULD
LOOK GOOD IN ANYTHING.

390
00:18:45,646 --> 00:18:47,517
THAT'S NOT THE POINT,
THOUGH, OKAY?

391
00:18:47,648 --> 00:18:50,694
ENJOY HIM
AND FOOL AROUND WITH HIM.

392
00:18:50,825 --> 00:18:52,566
DON'T FALL IN LOVE
WITH HIM.

393
00:18:52,696 --> 00:18:56,091
WHY DO YOU THINK THEY CALL IT
"FALLING," ANYWAYS?

394
00:18:56,222 --> 00:18:58,963
IT'S NOT WORTH IT TO YOU
TO SPEND MONEY ON A WEDDING.

395
00:18:59,094 --> 00:19:00,356
THE MOST IMPORTANT DAY.

396
00:19:00,487 --> 00:19:02,445
I WAS TRYING TO KILL
TWO BIRDS WITH ONE STONE.

397
00:19:02,576 --> 00:19:03,794
CHEAP IS WHAT THAT IS.

398
00:19:03,925 --> 00:19:06,275
OH, YOU SEE CHEAP,
I SEE CONVENIENCE.

399
00:19:06,406 --> 00:19:07,929
LOOK AT THEM.

400
00:19:08,059 --> 00:19:10,845
THEY'RE LIKE A WALKING
WARNING SIGN AGAINST ROMANCE.

401
00:19:10,975 --> 00:19:12,847
LEWIS IS THIS ANAL,
UPTIGHT GEEK

402
00:19:12,977 --> 00:19:15,197
WHO HAS MY SISTER
UNDER SOME KIND OF SPELL,

403
00:19:15,328 --> 00:19:17,678
SO NOW ALL THIS FORMERLY
SEMI-INTELLIGENT PERSON

404
00:19:17,808 --> 00:19:21,812
THINKS ABOUT IS DIAMONDS,
AND HAIRDOS...AND BULLSHIT.

405
00:19:21,943 --> 00:19:23,249
IT LOOKED LIKE A K-MART.

406
00:19:23,379 --> 00:19:25,338
HOW AM I SUPPOSED TO KNOW
BEFORE WE GO?

407
00:19:25,468 --> 00:19:27,470
MAYBE GO BY
AND LOOK AT IT.

408
00:19:27,601 --> 00:19:28,732
SEE? LOOK AT THEM.

409
00:19:28,863 --> 00:19:30,343
THEY DON'T
EVEN LIKE EACH OTHER,

410
00:19:30,473 --> 00:19:32,388
BUT BECAUSE OF THIS
STUPID SPELL THEY'RE UNDER,

411
00:19:32,519 --> 00:19:34,695
IT MAKES THEM DISREGARD
ALL THE FACTS.

412
00:19:34,825 --> 00:19:36,087
THEY ARE FIGHTING

413
00:19:36,218 --> 00:19:38,829
BECAUSE THEY LOVE EACH OTHER
ENOUGH TO CARE.

414
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:41,919
I DIDN'T KNOW IT LOOKED LIKE
A K-MART BEFORE I WENT THERE.

415
00:19:42,050 --> 00:19:43,747
LEWIS, ONCE WE GOT IN THERE,
YOU KNEW.

416
00:19:43,878 --> 00:19:45,445
OKAY, I GOOFED.

417
00:19:45,575 --> 00:19:47,838
TOO BAD YOU CAN'T GET A DIVORCE
BEFORE YOU GET MARRIED.

418
00:19:47,969 --> 00:19:49,318
THAT WAY,
YOU COULD SAVE YOURSELF

419
00:19:49,449 --> 00:19:51,712
ON THAT STUPID EXTRA STEP.

420
00:19:51,842 --> 00:19:54,541
LEWIS, I'M SORRY.

421
00:19:54,671 --> 00:19:56,195
SEE?

422
00:19:58,849 --> 00:20:00,155
Ashley: THESE DISHES,
THEY'RE PERFECT.

423
00:20:00,286 --> 00:20:04,551
AW...THAT'S LOVE, HALLEY.

424
00:20:04,681 --> 00:20:06,379
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

425
00:20:06,509 --> 00:20:09,338
FALL ONCE AND YOU MAY NEVER
BE ABLE TO GET BACK UP AGAIN.

426
00:20:09,469 --> 00:20:12,036
[ cell phone beeps ]

427
00:20:12,167 --> 00:20:13,647
MICHAEL.

428
00:20:15,431 --> 00:20:16,737
[ both laugh ]

429
00:20:16,867 --> 00:20:18,521
Halley: GEEK!
GET OUT OF HERE!

430
00:20:27,051 --> 00:20:29,271
ISN'T HE ADORABLE?

431
00:20:29,402 --> 00:20:30,359
HE'S CUTE.

432
00:20:34,494 --> 00:20:36,539
[ clapping and cheering ]

433
00:20:36,670 --> 00:20:38,933
YEAH! WHOO!

434
00:20:39,063 --> 00:20:40,239
YAY!

435
00:20:46,897 --> 00:20:48,116
ALL RIGHT, MICHAEL!

436
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:49,465
ALL RIGHT, MICHAEL!

437
00:20:49,596 --> 00:20:51,511
WAY TO GET THAT GOAL!

438
00:20:51,641 --> 00:20:52,642
WHOO!

439
00:20:59,693 --> 00:21:01,260
Coach: OKAY, GUYS,
LINE UP!

440
00:21:22,455 --> 00:21:23,891
Coach: ALL RIGHT, GUYS,
BACK UP.

441
00:21:24,021 --> 00:21:25,675
LET'S GIVE HIM SOME AIR.

442
00:21:25,806 --> 00:21:28,591
SHERWOOD?
SHERWOOD, YOU HEAR ME?

443
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:33,466
MICHAEL?

444
00:21:42,475 --> 00:21:44,303
GUYS, BACK UP.
GIVE HIM SOME AIR.

445
00:21:44,433 --> 00:21:46,130
ALL RIGHT?
A LITTLE BIT OF AIR.

446
00:21:46,261 --> 00:21:47,393
[ siren approaches ]

447
00:21:47,523 --> 00:21:48,829
CALL THE DOCTOR.

448
00:21:56,489 --> 00:22:01,537
I THOUGHT MY PARENTS' DIVORCE
WAS THE END OF THE WORLD.

449
00:22:01,668 --> 00:22:05,672
THAT WAS BEFORE MICHAEL DIED
OF A HEART DEFECT.

450
00:22:05,802 --> 00:22:08,283
AND THE WORLD STOPPED...

451
00:22:08,414 --> 00:22:10,720
OR IT SHOULD HAVE.

452
00:22:33,003 --> 00:22:34,353
I'M SORRY.

453
00:22:46,190 --> 00:22:47,235
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

454
00:22:48,628 --> 00:22:50,760
I THINK IT'S 100 DEGREES OUT.

455
00:22:54,895 --> 00:22:57,332
WHAT AM I SUPPOSED TO DO?

456
00:22:57,463 --> 00:23:00,291
THE ONLY BLACK CLOTHES I HAVE
ARE WINTER CLOTHES.

457
00:23:00,422 --> 00:23:02,468
I HAVE NOTHING NICE TO WEAR.

458
00:23:02,598 --> 00:23:04,687
I DON'T THINK
IT MATTERS, REALLY.

459
00:23:04,818 --> 00:23:06,297
LOOK, THIS IS...

460
00:23:06,428 --> 00:23:08,778
THIS IS DARK GREEN
AND IT'S REALLY NICE.

461
00:23:08,909 --> 00:23:10,519
IT'S UGLY, HALLEY.

462
00:23:14,088 --> 00:23:17,091
I'M JUST TRYING TO THINK
ABOUT SOMETHING ELSE.

463
00:23:17,221 --> 00:23:20,050
ANYTHING,
FOR ONE SINGLE SECOND.

464
00:23:34,891 --> 00:23:36,632
I WANNA LOOK GOOD FOR HIM.

465
00:23:39,026 --> 00:23:40,593
DOES THAT SOUND CRAZY?

466
00:23:41,942 --> 00:23:43,813
THIS WAS A BAD IDEA.

467
00:23:43,944 --> 00:23:48,296
YEAH, BUT DYING IS DEFINITELY
NOT ONE OF THE BETTER CONCEPTS.

468
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:49,645
NO, THE DRESS, HALLEY.

469
00:23:49,776 --> 00:23:51,517
EVERYONE'S LOOKING AT ME
LIKE I'M A FREAK.

470
00:23:51,647 --> 00:23:54,998
OKAY, IT'S NOT FOR THEM.
IT'S FOR MICHAEL.

471
00:23:55,129 --> 00:23:56,435
REMEMBER THAT.

472
00:23:58,306 --> 00:24:00,221
CAN YOU BELIEVE
WHAT SHE'S WEARING?

473
00:24:00,351 --> 00:24:02,832
THAT'S, LIKE,
SO DISRESPECTFUL.

474
00:24:02,963 --> 00:24:05,400
SHE ALWAYS HAS TO HAVE
ALL THE ATTENTION TO HERSELF.

475
00:24:07,707 --> 00:24:10,187
Pastor: "ALTHOUGH IT DROOP
AND DIE THAT NIGHT,

476
00:24:10,318 --> 00:24:15,366
"IT WAS THE PLANT
AND FLOWER OF LIGHT.

477
00:24:15,497 --> 00:24:20,241
"IN SMALL PROPORTIONS,
WE JUST BEAUTY SEE.

478
00:24:20,371 --> 00:24:22,286
"AND IN SHORT MEASURES,

479
00:24:22,417 --> 00:24:26,247
LIFE MAY PERFECT BE."

480
00:24:29,511 --> 00:24:32,819
MR. MACON FORRESTER
WILL NOW ADDRESS US.

481
00:24:52,403 --> 00:24:54,884
I--I WAS GONNA
READ FROM THIS...

482
00:24:59,323 --> 00:25:00,977
BUT I'M NOT VERY GOOD
AT READING.

483
00:25:03,545 --> 00:25:05,504
OR WRITING...

484
00:25:05,634 --> 00:25:08,724
OR SPELLING.

485
00:25:08,855 --> 00:25:11,379
NOT LIKE MICHAEL.

486
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:14,164
HE WAS GOOD AT SO MANY THINGS
WITHOUT EVEN TRYING.

487
00:25:16,253 --> 00:25:19,605
HE TAUGHT ME
HOW TO BE MYSELF...

488
00:25:19,735 --> 00:25:20,823
BY MYSELF.

489
00:25:23,739 --> 00:25:26,263
AND NOT TO WORRY
ABOUT WHAT OTHER PEOPLE THINK.

490
00:25:28,396 --> 00:25:31,007
EVEN IF THAT MEANS
BEING COMPLETELY UNCOOL.

491
00:25:33,967 --> 00:25:37,623
HE TAUGHT ME ABOUT
HOW TO TRUST PEOPLE.

492
00:25:41,496 --> 00:25:44,760
AND HOW TO LOVE.

493
00:25:44,891 --> 00:25:46,240
'CAUSE HE WAS SO GOOD.

494
00:25:46,370 --> 00:25:49,025
HE LOVED HIS FAMILY,
HE LOVED HIS FRIENDS.

495
00:25:49,156 --> 00:25:51,375
HE LOVED BASKETBALL.

496
00:25:52,725 --> 00:25:54,683
AND HE LOVED SCARLETT.

497
00:25:58,731 --> 00:26:01,560
AND HE LOVED THIS.

498
00:26:01,690 --> 00:26:03,736
[ plays "Do You Realize,"
by the Flaming Lips ]

499
00:26:03,866 --> 00:26:11,178
♪ DO YOU REALIZE

500
00:26:11,308 --> 00:26:20,361
♪ THAT YOU HAVE
THE MOST BEAUTIFUL FACE? ♪

501
00:26:20,491 --> 00:26:25,888
♪ DO YOU REALIZE

502
00:26:26,019 --> 00:26:28,151
[ thunder crashes ]

503
00:26:31,154 --> 00:26:35,158
♪ WE'RE FLOATING IN SPACE?

504
00:26:35,289 --> 00:26:39,467
♪ DO YOU REALIZE

505
00:26:44,037 --> 00:26:49,912
♪ THAT HAPPINESS
MAKES YOU CRY? ♪

506
00:26:50,043 --> 00:26:54,177
♪ DO YOU REALIZE

507
00:27:02,838 --> 00:27:04,884
♪♪

508
00:27:05,014 --> 00:27:07,800
♪ YOUR LOVE
IS LIKE A CAR CRASH ♪

509
00:27:07,930 --> 00:27:10,846
♪ DON'T IT ALL THAT WHIPLASH?

510
00:27:10,977 --> 00:27:14,110
♪ YOU'RE A STAIN
I CAN'T GET OUT ♪

511
00:27:14,241 --> 00:27:16,765
♪ I TRY BLEACH
AND I TRY SHOUT ♪

512
00:27:16,896 --> 00:27:18,637
♪ YOU'RE THE KIND OF GUY

513
00:27:18,767 --> 00:27:21,465
♪ WHO NEEDS ATTENTION
AROUND THE CLOCK ♪

514
00:27:21,596 --> 00:27:23,729
Man: ...TAKE THIS WOMAN,
LORNA QUEEN,

515
00:27:23,859 --> 00:27:25,774
TO BE YOUR LAWFUL WEDDED WIFE,
YOUR PARTNER

516
00:27:25,905 --> 00:27:27,776
THE QUEEN OF YOUR OWN HEART,
FOREVER AND EVER?

517
00:27:27,907 --> 00:27:28,908
OH, YEAH!

518
00:27:29,038 --> 00:27:30,649
DADDY, ROCK ON
WITH YOUR WOMAN!

519
00:27:30,779 --> 00:27:32,520
[ cheering and barking ]

520
00:27:32,651 --> 00:27:35,305
AND DO YOU,
LORNA P. QUEEN,

521
00:27:35,436 --> 00:27:38,308
TAKE THIS OLD GUY LEN TO BE
YOUR LAWFUL WEDDED HUSBAND

522
00:27:38,439 --> 00:27:40,441
FOR ALL THE REST OF YOUR DAYS?

523
00:27:40,571 --> 00:27:41,442
I DO.

524
00:27:41,572 --> 00:27:44,663
[ cheering ]

525
00:27:45,838 --> 00:27:48,101
WRAP IT UP.
WE'RE OFF IN 15 SECONDS.

526
00:27:48,231 --> 00:27:50,277
OUR AIRTIME IS ALMOST UP.

527
00:27:50,407 --> 00:27:51,800
WOO-WOO!

528
00:27:51,931 --> 00:27:55,282
WE MUST NOW GO
WHERE FEDERAL REGULATIONS

529
00:27:55,412 --> 00:27:59,721
WILL NOT ALLOW YOU TO FOLLOW,
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

530
00:27:59,852 --> 00:28:01,070
[ howls ]

531
00:28:01,201 --> 00:28:02,376
[ barks ]

532
00:28:02,506 --> 00:28:04,770
LEWIS, NO!
NO BARKING.

533
00:28:05,988 --> 00:28:08,556
♪ THEN A TALL GLASS
OF BUD DRY ♪

534
00:28:08,687 --> 00:28:10,601
♪ WELL,
YOU'RE THE KIND OF GUY ♪

535
00:28:10,732 --> 00:28:13,561
♪ WHO NEEDS ATTENTION
AROUND THE CLOCK ♪

536
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:20,611
SORRY, BUT YOU GOTTA GO.

537
00:28:22,701 --> 00:28:25,355
OH, POOR LITTLE THING.

538
00:28:25,486 --> 00:28:28,315
I KNOW JUST HOW IT FEELS.

539
00:28:28,445 --> 00:28:31,100
OUT WITH THE OLD,
IN WITH THE NEW.

540
00:28:33,755 --> 00:28:35,844
AND WHO DO YOU THINK YOU ARE?

541
00:28:35,975 --> 00:28:38,107
JUST BECAUSE
YOU'VE GOT GREAT PETALS.

542
00:28:40,849 --> 00:28:44,026
OH, MY GOD.
I'M TALKING TO MY PLANTS.

543
00:28:44,157 --> 00:28:46,072
OH, MY GOD.

544
00:28:46,202 --> 00:28:47,943
YOU'RE TALKING
TO YOUR PLANTS.

545
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:52,165
HOW WAS IT?

546
00:28:52,295 --> 00:28:53,862
IT WAS GREAT...

547
00:28:53,993 --> 00:28:57,474
IF YOU HAPPEN TO BE THE DEVIL
AND ENJOY HUMAN PAIN.

548
00:28:57,605 --> 00:28:59,215
TELL ME SOMETHING.

549
00:28:59,346 --> 00:29:00,477
I DON'T KNOW!

550
00:29:00,608 --> 00:29:02,262
WHAT DO YOU WANT ME
TO TELL YOU?

551
00:29:02,392 --> 00:29:05,178
WAIT! NO, THE BIMBO
ALMOST DIED OF STRANGULATION.

552
00:29:05,308 --> 00:29:07,180
I CANNOT BELIEVE
I FORGOT TO TELL YOU.

553
00:29:07,310 --> 00:29:10,313
HER WEDDING VEIL TOOK ON
A LIFE OF ITS OWN AND REBELLED.

554
00:29:10,444 --> 00:29:12,663
AND SHE HAD TO CLAW
HER WAY OUT.

555
00:29:12,794 --> 00:29:14,665
AND YOU KNOW
THAT WOMAN CAN CLAW, MOM.

556
00:29:14,796 --> 00:29:15,971
IT WAS SO SAD.

557
00:29:16,102 --> 00:29:18,452
IT WAS LIKE,
NEAR DEATH BY WEDDING VEIL.

558
00:29:18,582 --> 00:29:20,106
OH...

559
00:29:20,236 --> 00:29:22,021
JUST TRAGIC, ISN'T IT?

560
00:29:22,151 --> 00:29:24,545
OH, MY GOD!
AND THEIR VOWS?

561
00:29:24,675 --> 00:29:27,635
WAS DAD THAT MUCH A LOSER
WHEN YOU GUYS GOT MARRIED?

562
00:29:29,811 --> 00:29:30,943
I'M SORRY.

563
00:29:37,210 --> 00:29:38,907
YOUR FATHER'S NOT A LOSER.

564
00:29:41,562 --> 00:29:45,131
ALTHOUGH HE DID CHOOSE TO LOOK
LIKE ONE AT OUR WEDDING, TOO.

565
00:29:45,261 --> 00:29:48,395
HE INSISTED ON WEARING
A POWDER-BLUE TUXEDO.

566
00:29:58,057 --> 00:30:00,581
THEN WHY DO PEOPLE
GET MARRIED, ANYWAYS?

567
00:30:00,711 --> 00:30:02,713
I MEAN, WE KNOW
THEY'RE LYING TO EACH OTHER,

568
00:30:02,844 --> 00:30:04,933
BUT ARE THEY LYING
TO THEMSELVES, TOO?

569
00:30:06,500 --> 00:30:09,329
HOW CAN YOU PROMISE YOU'RE GONNA
FEEL THE SAME WAY FOREVER?

570
00:30:14,595 --> 00:30:16,858
THINGS DO
SOMETIMES CHANGE, HALLEY.

571
00:30:21,428 --> 00:30:24,735
THIS HOUSE IS AWFULLY BIG
FOR JUST THE TWO OF US,

572
00:30:24,866 --> 00:30:26,172
DON'T YOU THINK?

573
00:30:27,477 --> 00:30:28,435
WHAT?

574
00:30:28,565 --> 00:30:30,089
YOU'LL BE GOING
TO COLLEGE SOON.

575
00:30:30,219 --> 00:30:33,266
MOM...A YEAR AND 3/4
IS NOT REALLY THAT SOON.

576
00:30:33,396 --> 00:30:35,703
I WANT US TO START THINKING
ABOUT STREAMLINING, HALLEY.

577
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:37,531
MAYBE WE SHOULD SELL
THE HOUSE.

578
00:30:39,185 --> 00:30:40,621
I GREW UP IN THIS HOUSE.

579
00:30:40,751 --> 00:30:43,580
YES, AND THERE HAVE BEEN
GREAT MEMORIES IN THIS HOUSE.

580
00:30:43,711 --> 00:30:45,104
THIS IS MY HOUSE.

581
00:30:45,234 --> 00:30:48,542
I UNDERSTAND HOW YOU MUST FEEL,
BUT LIFE CHANGES.

582
00:30:48,672 --> 00:30:51,588
THIS IS RIDICULOUS,
MOM, COME ON!

583
00:30:56,332 --> 00:30:59,553
AND I DON'T WANT
TO LIVE HERE ALONE.

584
00:31:14,611 --> 00:31:17,571
[ indistinct conversation ]

585
00:31:23,098 --> 00:31:23,882
BYE, HALLEY.

586
00:31:24,012 --> 00:31:25,013
BYE, HALLEY.

587
00:31:26,623 --> 00:31:28,756
[ boy imitates dramatic music ]

588
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:30,801
STAND BACK!
LEAF MAN TO THE RESCUE.

589
00:31:32,238 --> 00:31:33,848
WHERE DID YOU GET THAT?

590
00:31:33,979 --> 00:31:37,199
A GUY'S GOTTA PAY FOR GAS
AND BACON BURGERS SOMEHOW.

591
00:31:37,330 --> 00:31:38,897
AND TOYS, 'CAUSE I IMAGINE

592
00:31:39,027 --> 00:31:41,464
STAR WARSFIGURINES
MUST GET PRETTY EXPENSIVE.

593
00:31:41,595 --> 00:31:43,727
I DO NOT HAVE
ANY STAR WARSFIGURINES.

594
00:31:43,858 --> 00:31:47,340
WELL...NOT MANY,
AND I DON'T PLAY WITH THEM...

595
00:31:47,470 --> 00:31:49,037
MUCH.

596
00:31:49,168 --> 00:31:50,473
THIS ONE'S ON THE HOUSE.

597
00:31:52,562 --> 00:31:53,476
OKAY.

598
00:31:53,607 --> 00:31:55,000
UH-HUH.

599
00:31:55,130 --> 00:31:56,305
HERE YOU GO.

600
00:32:00,266 --> 00:32:01,832
YOU'RE AFRAID
TO GO OUT WITH ME

601
00:32:01,963 --> 00:32:03,530
BECAUSE YOU ACTUALLY
MIGHT LIKE ME?

602
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:06,663
NO, BUT THAT'S
A GOOD THEORY, I GUESS,

603
00:32:06,794 --> 00:32:09,492
IF YOU WANT TO PROTECT
YOUR FRAGILE MALE EGO.

604
00:32:09,623 --> 00:32:11,494
'CAUSE YOU CAN'T
HANDLE REJECTION!

605
00:32:11,625 --> 00:32:13,322
REJECTION? WHATEVER!

606
00:32:15,150 --> 00:32:18,284
♪ GET A LOAD OF ME
GET A LOAD OF YOU ♪

607
00:32:18,414 --> 00:32:21,809
♪ WALKING DOWN THE STREET
AND I HARDLY KNOW YOU ♪

608
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:23,332
♪ HARDLY KNOW YOU

609
00:32:23,463 --> 00:32:27,075
♪ IT'S JUST LIKE
WE WERE MEANT TO BE ♪

610
00:32:27,206 --> 00:32:29,556
♪ WHAT IT IS
IS JUST THE BEGINNING ♪

611
00:32:29,686 --> 00:32:33,560
♪ WE'RE ALREADY WET
AND WE'RE GONNA GO SWIMMING ♪

612
00:32:33,690 --> 00:32:36,258
♪ WHY CAN'T I BREATHE

613
00:32:36,389 --> 00:32:39,522
♪ WHENEVER I THINK
ABOUT YOU? ♪

614
00:32:39,653 --> 00:32:42,351
♪ WHY CAN'T I SPEAK

615
00:32:42,482 --> 00:32:44,832
♪ WHENEVER
I TALK ABOUT YOU? ♪

616
00:32:44,963 --> 00:32:46,486
♪ IT'S INEVITABLE

617
00:32:46,616 --> 00:32:49,576
♪ IT'S A FACT THAT WE'RE
GONNA GET DOWN TO IT ♪

618
00:32:49,706 --> 00:32:51,273
♪ SO TELL ME

619
00:32:51,404 --> 00:32:54,233
♪ WHY CAN'T I BREATHE

620
00:32:54,363 --> 00:32:57,149
♪ WHENEVER I THINK
ABOUT YOU? ♪

621
00:32:57,279 --> 00:33:00,065
♪ WHENEVER
I THINK ABOUT YOU ♪

622
00:33:00,195 --> 00:33:02,415
♪ WHENEVER I THINK
ABOUT YOU ♪

623
00:33:02,545 --> 00:33:04,983
[ soft tapping ]

624
00:33:20,911 --> 00:33:22,565
[ sound continues ]

625
00:33:32,706 --> 00:33:34,186
OF COURSE
YOU THINK IT'S WEIRD

626
00:33:34,316 --> 00:33:36,101
THAT I DIDN'T
JUST USE THE PHONE,

627
00:33:36,231 --> 00:33:37,580
BUT YOU'RE ALSO GLAD

628
00:33:37,711 --> 00:33:39,626
BECAUSE IT'S SO MUCH BETTER
TO TALK IN PERSON.

629
00:33:39,756 --> 00:33:42,455
ESPECIALLY WHEN I'VE COME
WITH SUCH A SPECIFIC PURPOSE.

630
00:33:43,934 --> 00:33:46,198
WHICH IS WHY YOU'RE
GONNA CUT ME SOME SLACK HERE.

631
00:33:48,852 --> 00:33:50,637
YOU ARE ABSOLUTELY CRAZY.

632
00:33:50,767 --> 00:33:52,595
I'VE BEEN CALLED WORSE.

633
00:33:53,988 --> 00:33:55,424
YOU'RE GONNA KISS ME,
HALLEY.

634
00:33:57,861 --> 00:33:59,863
YOU'RE GONNA COME
A LITTLE CLOSER...

635
00:34:06,218 --> 00:34:08,176
SO I CAN PUT
MY ARMS AROUND YOU.

636
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:11,745
AND THEN,
ON THE COUNT OF THREE...

637
00:34:13,442 --> 00:34:15,488
TWO...

638
00:34:15,618 --> 00:34:16,619
ONE.

639
00:34:30,155 --> 00:34:32,244
YOU'RE A REALLY
GOOD KISSER.

640
00:34:33,854 --> 00:34:36,335
YOU TRICKED ME.

641
00:34:36,465 --> 00:34:39,468
YOU JEDI MIND-TRICKED ME.

642
00:34:39,599 --> 00:34:40,426
[ door opens ]

643
00:34:40,556 --> 00:34:41,601
HALLEY?

644
00:34:43,864 --> 00:34:45,300
HALLEY, IS THAT YOU OUT THERE?

645
00:34:45,431 --> 00:34:48,347
Macon [whispering]:
Close your eyes, go to bed.

646
00:34:48,477 --> 00:34:49,304
Gimme a break.

647
00:34:49,435 --> 00:34:51,089
WHO ARE YOU TALKING TO?

648
00:34:53,308 --> 00:34:54,222
Halley: UM...

649
00:34:54,353 --> 00:34:56,137
I'M SORRY, I, UM...

650
00:34:56,268 --> 00:34:58,139
SORRY.

651
00:34:58,270 --> 00:35:01,534
I JUST...
I NEEDED TO TALK.

652
00:35:02,970 --> 00:35:06,278
I WAS JUST COMING OVER
FOR A LITTLE LATE-NIGHT CHAT.

653
00:35:07,714 --> 00:35:10,717
WE'RE NOT GONNA STAY UP
VERY LATE, THOUGH. OKAY?

654
00:35:10,847 --> 00:35:12,327
AT LEAST DO IT INSIDE.

655
00:35:17,202 --> 00:35:18,377
"NAUSEA"?

656
00:35:19,856 --> 00:35:22,076
A LITTLE.

657
00:35:22,207 --> 00:35:23,991
"BREAST TENDERNESS"?

658
00:35:26,472 --> 00:35:28,256
OW.

659
00:35:28,387 --> 00:35:30,302
YEAH. MAJOR.

660
00:35:30,432 --> 00:35:31,825
"FOOD CRAVINGS"?

661
00:35:40,007 --> 00:35:41,051
GRAPEFRUIT.

662
00:35:41,182 --> 00:35:42,575
SCARLETT, COME ON,

663
00:35:42,705 --> 00:35:45,839
I COULD ANSWER "YES" TO MOST
OF THESE QUESTIONS, TOO.

664
00:35:45,969 --> 00:35:47,841
I USED TO HATE GRAPEFRUIT.

665
00:35:51,932 --> 00:35:53,107
WHAT'S WRONG?

666
00:35:55,979 --> 00:35:57,633
NO OFFENSE, HALLEY,
BUT...

667
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:01,942
UGH...YOUR PERFUME
IS MAKING ME SICK.

668
00:36:02,072 --> 00:36:03,770
OH, COME ON,
I'M NOT WEARING PERFUME.

669
00:36:03,900 --> 00:36:05,119
I USE SOAP.

670
00:36:05,250 --> 00:36:06,381
MM-HM.

671
00:36:12,431 --> 00:36:15,173
"HEIGHTENED SENSE OF SMELL."

672
00:36:15,303 --> 00:36:17,958
OKAY, SO DO YOU PREFER
DIRECT PEE-ON-A-STRIP

673
00:36:18,088 --> 00:36:18,959
OR DIP-IN-A-CUP?

674
00:36:19,089 --> 00:36:20,221
SHH!

675
00:36:22,919 --> 00:36:24,617
Halley:
MAYBE IT'S A FALSE READING.

676
00:36:24,747 --> 00:36:27,924
BECAUSE I HAVE HEARD OF THINGS
SUCH AS FALSE READINGS,

677
00:36:28,055 --> 00:36:30,057
AND THE STRIPS DID NOT
LOOK COMPLETELY PINK,

678
00:36:30,188 --> 00:36:31,928
THEY LOOKED ONLY
KIND OF PINKISH, SO--

679
00:36:32,059 --> 00:36:33,887
FIVE KITS, HALLEY.

680
00:36:41,460 --> 00:36:43,070
WHAT AM I GONNA DO?

681
00:36:54,255 --> 00:36:55,561
[ honks horn ]

682
00:37:01,262 --> 00:37:03,830
SO YOU TAKE THE CAR
WITHOUT MY PERMISSION

683
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:06,572
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE NIGHT
ON SOME KIND OF JOY RIDE.

684
00:37:06,702 --> 00:37:07,877
IT WASN'T A JOY RIDE.

685
00:37:08,008 --> 00:37:09,401
MAYBE I SHOULD--

686
00:37:09,531 --> 00:37:12,142
DON'T THINK YOU'RE
OFF THE HOOK, HALLEY MARTIN.

687
00:37:12,273 --> 00:37:13,970
YOU DON'T EVEN HAVE
YOUR DRIVER'S LICENSE,

688
00:37:14,101 --> 00:37:15,842
AND YOU ARE
A TERRIBLE DRIVER.

689
00:37:15,972 --> 00:37:18,061
I WAS HELPING SCARLETT
GET SOME BOOKS AT SCHOOL.

690
00:37:18,192 --> 00:37:19,019
WE LEFT THEM THERE--

691
00:37:19,149 --> 00:37:21,021
FORGET IT, HALLEY!

692
00:37:21,151 --> 00:37:23,371
MOM...

693
00:37:23,502 --> 00:37:24,633
TAKING YOUR CAR OUT

694
00:37:24,764 --> 00:37:27,245
IS GONNA SEEM
LIKE THE LEAST OF IT.

695
00:37:27,375 --> 00:37:31,336
BECAUSE WHATEVER YOU'RE
THINKING RIGHT NOW...

696
00:37:31,466 --> 00:37:33,120
IT'S WORSE.

697
00:37:37,385 --> 00:37:39,126
WELL, ONE OF YOU
BETTER TELL ME

698
00:37:39,257 --> 00:37:41,346
BEFORE I HAVE
A NERVOUS BREAKDOWN.

699
00:37:51,356 --> 00:37:52,835
I'M PREGNANT.

700
00:38:01,931 --> 00:38:04,238
WELL, THANK GOD
YOU TOLD ME IN TIME.

701
00:38:06,196 --> 00:38:09,199
[ cries softly ]

702
00:38:12,942 --> 00:38:15,858
SHOULDN'T I BE GETTING PAID
TO WEAR A DRESS THIS UGLY?

703
00:38:15,989 --> 00:38:17,643
I'M SORRY
IF YOU HATE MY TASTE

704
00:38:17,773 --> 00:38:20,776
AND YOU THINK IT'S SO AWFUL
YOU HAVE TO BE IN MY WEDDING,

705
00:38:20,907 --> 00:38:22,082
BUT YOU ARE MY SISTER.

706
00:38:22,212 --> 00:38:23,388
Woman:
IT'S AN EMOTIONAL TIME.

707
00:38:23,518 --> 00:38:25,128
ALL RIGHT,
I WAS JUST JOKING.

708
00:38:25,259 --> 00:38:27,696
JUST BECAUSE YOU THINK UP
SOMETHING YOU THINK IS FUNNY,

709
00:38:27,827 --> 00:38:29,785
DOESN'T MEAN
YOU HAVE TO SAY IT.

710
00:38:29,916 --> 00:38:33,136
OKAY, ASHLEY,
I'M SORRY, ALL RIGHT?

711
00:38:33,267 --> 00:38:34,442
IT'S JUST...

712
00:38:34,573 --> 00:38:36,531
I LOVE THE DRESS, REALLY.

713
00:38:36,662 --> 00:38:39,186
I FEEL LIKE A PRINCESS,
YOU KNOW?

714
00:38:43,973 --> 00:38:45,497
[ sighs ]

715
00:38:47,194 --> 00:38:48,326
I LOOK AWFUL.

716
00:38:49,718 --> 00:38:50,893
WE'LL FIX IT.

717
00:38:51,024 --> 00:38:52,852
IT'S NOT THE DRESS
THAT NEEDS FIXING.

718
00:38:52,982 --> 00:38:55,245
IT'S ME.

719
00:38:55,376 --> 00:38:57,944
ASHLEY, WOULD YOU
DRIVE HALLEY HOME?

720
00:38:58,074 --> 00:39:00,250
'CAUSE I HAVE
TO GET BACK TO WORK.

721
00:39:18,704 --> 00:39:19,966
GIVE ME MY MONEY BACK,

722
00:39:20,096 --> 00:39:22,925
YOU STUPID, LYING, FECKLESS,

723
00:39:23,056 --> 00:39:25,363
TWO-TIMING
SON OF A BITCH!

724
00:39:28,453 --> 00:39:30,063
CAN I HELP YOU, MA'AM?

725
00:39:39,115 --> 00:39:42,075
IT STOLE MY MONEY,
SO, JUST...

726
00:39:43,076 --> 00:39:44,164
HERE.

727
00:39:44,294 --> 00:39:47,080
THIS WORKS
A LITTLE BETTER SOMETIMES.

728
00:39:56,481 --> 00:39:57,351
WHAT'S YOUR PLEASURE?

729
00:39:57,482 --> 00:39:59,832
DIET COKE SOUNDS GOOD.

730
00:39:59,962 --> 00:40:01,311
THE LAST ONE.

731
00:40:06,142 --> 00:40:07,187
ON ME.

732
00:40:08,580 --> 00:40:11,626
I HOPE I DIDN'T,
YOU KNOW, KICK IT TOO...

733
00:40:11,757 --> 00:40:14,020
I THINK THESE MACHINES
ARE BUILT

734
00:40:14,150 --> 00:40:17,327
TO WITHSTAND A GOOD BOOTING
EVERY NOW AND THEN.

735
00:40:18,633 --> 00:40:19,678
STEVE BECKWITH.

736
00:40:19,808 --> 00:40:21,419
LYDIA MARTIN.

737
00:40:21,549 --> 00:40:23,203
DID I SAY "MARTIN"?

738
00:40:23,333 --> 00:40:25,118
IT'S LYDIA WILLIAMS NOW.

739
00:40:25,248 --> 00:40:26,554
LYDIA WILLIAMS AGAIN.

740
00:40:26,685 --> 00:40:28,469
WILLIAMS. AGAIN.

741
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:29,862
LYDIA.

742
00:40:29,992 --> 00:40:31,341
NICE TO MEET YOU.

743
00:40:35,258 --> 00:40:36,608
THANK YOU.

744
00:40:38,653 --> 00:40:40,612
AREN'T YOU GONNA WEAR
ANY LIPSTICK?

745
00:40:40,742 --> 00:40:42,178
YOU SOUND LIKE MOM.

746
00:40:42,309 --> 00:40:45,094
CAN ONE OF YOU TWO
ZIP ME, PLEASE?

747
00:40:45,225 --> 00:40:49,011
OKAY, YOU GUYS KNOW YOU'RE
WEARING THE SAME DRESS, RIGHT?

748
00:40:49,142 --> 00:40:50,012
UNBELIEVABLE.

749
00:40:50,143 --> 00:40:51,753
[ knocks on door ]

750
00:40:51,884 --> 00:40:53,538
DON'T USE THAT BATHROOM.
YOU'RE GRANDMOTHER'S IN THERE.

751
00:40:53,668 --> 00:40:54,582
WE PRACTICALLY ARE.

752
00:40:54,713 --> 00:40:55,583
I'LL CHANGE.

753
00:40:55,714 --> 00:40:56,889
NO, I'LL CHANGE.
I'LL CHANGE.

754
00:40:57,019 --> 00:40:58,064
I CAN CHANGE.

755
00:40:58,194 --> 00:40:59,369
NO, I SHOULDN'T
WEAR BLACK ANYWAYS.

756
00:40:59,500 --> 00:41:01,371
HALLEY, COULD YOU
PLEASE JUST WEAR

757
00:41:01,502 --> 00:41:02,938
SOMETHING A LITTLE BIT
MORE FEMININE

758
00:41:03,069 --> 00:41:05,027
BECAUSE THE WARSHERS
ARE REALLY TRADITIONAL.

759
00:41:05,158 --> 00:41:06,376
THANK YOU.

760
00:41:06,507 --> 00:41:09,771
SWEETHEART...
DO YOU NEED THE LOO?

761
00:41:09,902 --> 00:41:11,077
OH, GRANDMA, NO, NO, NO.

762
00:41:11,207 --> 00:41:12,905
I'M GONNA USE
THE ONE DOWNSTAIRS.

763
00:41:13,035 --> 00:41:14,646
DON'T BE SILLY.

764
00:41:14,776 --> 00:41:16,386
UH, COME ON IN.

765
00:41:16,517 --> 00:41:17,431
OKAY.

766
00:41:17,562 --> 00:41:18,824
I'M ALMOST THROUGH.

767
00:41:29,748 --> 00:41:31,358
IT SMELLS LIKE, UM...

768
00:41:34,709 --> 00:41:35,667
OH.

769
00:41:36,972 --> 00:41:39,409
JUST BURNING
A LITTLE INCENSE.

770
00:41:39,540 --> 00:41:40,454
[ knock on door ]

771
00:41:40,585 --> 00:41:41,890
MOTHER?

772
00:41:43,544 --> 00:41:45,503
ARE YOU SMOKING
THE CANNABIS AGAIN?

773
00:41:46,808 --> 00:41:49,724
I HAD A LITTLE HEADACHE.

774
00:41:49,855 --> 00:41:52,988
BUT I'M FEELING
REALLY MUCH BETTER NOW.

775
00:41:59,255 --> 00:42:00,430
I KNEW WE'D BE LATE.

776
00:42:00,561 --> 00:42:01,693
WE'RE FINE.

777
00:42:04,870 --> 00:42:07,394
HIS PARENTS
ARE PROMPTNESS NUTS.

778
00:42:07,525 --> 00:42:09,614
I CAN'T BELIEVE I'M LATE.

779
00:42:09,744 --> 00:42:10,876
ASHLEY, THAT'S WHAT HAPPENS

780
00:42:11,006 --> 00:42:13,052
WHEN YOU MAKE PEOPLE CHANGE
TEN TIMES.

781
00:42:14,575 --> 00:42:15,794
OOH...

782
00:42:15,924 --> 00:42:19,624
THESE LEAVES WOULD MAKE
A WONDERFUL TEXTILE.

783
00:42:19,754 --> 00:42:21,713
HALLEY, LOOK.

784
00:42:21,843 --> 00:42:23,279
I'LL BET
IF WE MAKE SHEETS...

785
00:42:23,410 --> 00:42:25,368
MOTHER!

786
00:42:25,499 --> 00:42:28,241
OF THIS PATTERN,
WE'D MAKE A MILLION DOLLARS!

787
00:42:28,371 --> 00:42:30,548
MOTHER, PLEASE, NOT NOW.

788
00:42:32,898 --> 00:42:33,986
[ whispers ]
She's high.

789
00:42:34,116 --> 00:42:36,771
SHE'S NOT HIGH,
SHE'S MEDICATED.

790
00:42:36,902 --> 00:42:38,468
OW.

791
00:42:39,513 --> 00:42:40,558
Grandma: "OW"...

792
00:42:40,688 --> 00:42:41,994
YOU KNOW,
IT'S INTERESTING--

793
00:42:42,124 --> 00:42:43,952
WHEN YOU MAKE
THE "OW" SOUND,

794
00:42:44,083 --> 00:42:46,433
YOUR MOUTH DOES
THIS FUNNY THING

795
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:47,608
IN THE CORNERS.

796
00:42:47,739 --> 00:42:49,175
MOTHER,
YOU'RE NOT SICK ANYMORE.

797
00:42:49,305 --> 00:42:51,046
YOU WERE ONLY ALLOWED
TO USE WEED WHEN YOU WERE SICK.

798
00:42:51,177 --> 00:42:52,047
YOU'RE NOT SICK ANYMORE.

799
00:42:52,178 --> 00:42:53,309
I DO HAVE
HEADACHES A LOT.

800
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:54,833
SHE'LL BE FINE.
WOULD YOU RING THE BELL?

801
00:42:54,963 --> 00:42:55,877
SMILE.

802
00:42:56,008 --> 00:42:57,139
[ doorbell chimes ]

803
00:42:57,270 --> 00:42:58,663
DOES ANYONE ELSE
HEAR WIND CHIMES,

804
00:42:58,793 --> 00:43:00,229
OR IS IT JUST ME?

805
00:43:00,360 --> 00:43:01,753
THIS IS A TOTAL DISASTER.

806
00:43:02,797 --> 00:43:03,755
SHIT!

807
00:43:08,063 --> 00:43:09,238
HELLO.

808
00:43:11,023 --> 00:43:12,633
I KNOW IT'S TURKEY DAY,

809
00:43:12,764 --> 00:43:15,201
BUT WE THOUGHT SQUAB
WOULD BE MOST SPECIAL.

810
00:43:15,331 --> 00:43:17,943
OH, THEY'RE
ABSOLUTELY ADORABLE.

811
00:43:19,466 --> 00:43:21,033
SQUAB.

812
00:43:21,163 --> 00:43:22,556
CAN I SAY
I'M A VEGETARIAN?

813
00:43:22,687 --> 00:43:23,905
NO.

814
00:43:24,036 --> 00:43:25,951
IT REMINDS ME OF A LITTLE
YELLOW PARAKEET

815
00:43:26,081 --> 00:43:28,649
I HAD WHEN I WAS A GIRL.

816
00:43:28,780 --> 00:43:32,392
SUCH A SWEET,
SMART LITTLE BIRD.

817
00:43:33,698 --> 00:43:34,612
THEY LOOK WONDERFUL.

818
00:43:34,742 --> 00:43:35,874
THANK YOU.

819
00:43:36,004 --> 00:43:39,138
MARCELLA'S SUCH A TRULY
MAGNIFICENT COOK.

820
00:43:39,268 --> 00:43:41,183
WE ARE LUCKY
TO HAVE FOUND HER.

821
00:43:41,314 --> 00:43:43,577
OH, I BET THERE'S
A STORY IN THAT.

822
00:43:43,708 --> 00:43:45,231
TELL ME,
HOW LOST WERE YOU

823
00:43:45,361 --> 00:43:47,450
BEFORE YOU WERE FOUND?

824
00:43:47,581 --> 00:43:52,368
BECAUSE YOU LOOK LIKE A LADY
WHO DOESN'T GET LOST VERY OFTEN.

825
00:43:52,499 --> 00:43:54,109
GRANDMA.

826
00:43:54,240 --> 00:43:55,894
SHE CAME WITH US 20 YEARS AGO

827
00:43:56,024 --> 00:43:57,635
WHEN WE MOVED UP HERE
FROM ATLANTA.

828
00:43:58,679 --> 00:44:00,812
SHE REALLY RAISED OUR LEWIS.

829
00:44:03,118 --> 00:44:05,338
I DIDN'T REALIZE
YOU WERE A WORKING MOTHER.

830
00:44:07,253 --> 00:44:08,776
I WASN'T.

831
00:44:08,907 --> 00:44:12,214
SHE DID GO THROUGH
A BROKERAGE TRAINING PROGRAM.

832
00:44:12,345 --> 00:44:13,651
SHE WAS GOOD.

833
00:44:13,781 --> 00:44:15,391
KILLER INSTINCT.

834
00:44:15,522 --> 00:44:17,785
BUT SHE SET HER SIGHTS
ON ME, INSTEAD.

835
00:44:17,916 --> 00:44:20,745
AND I'D SAY I GOT
THE BEST DEAL AT THE FIRM.

836
00:44:20,875 --> 00:44:22,094
HE'S ALL RIGHT.

837
00:44:22,224 --> 00:44:23,965
HE'S NO CLARK GABLE,

838
00:44:24,096 --> 00:44:26,968
BUT THEN
VERY FEW MEN ARE.

839
00:44:27,099 --> 00:44:29,928
WHAT WAS THE NAME
OF THAT CHARACTER?

840
00:44:30,058 --> 00:44:30,885
ASHLEY.

841
00:44:31,016 --> 00:44:32,844
ASHLEY.

842
00:44:32,974 --> 00:44:34,628
NO, YOU'RE ASHLEY.

843
00:44:37,283 --> 00:44:38,850
[ chuckles nervously ]

844
00:44:40,808 --> 00:44:42,854
THE WEDDING PLANS
ARE COMING ALONG BEAUTIFULLY.

845
00:44:42,984 --> 00:44:45,639
OH, WELL, YOU HOLLER
IF YOU NEED ANY HELP AT ALL.

846
00:44:45,770 --> 00:44:48,816
I WANT THIS TO BE
A MEMORABLE AFFAIR.

847
00:44:48,947 --> 00:44:51,297
Mr. Warsher: CAROL DOES THROW
ON HECK OF A LUNCHEON.

848
00:44:51,427 --> 00:44:53,212
Mrs. Warsher:
THAT IS MY ONE REGRET

849
00:44:53,342 --> 00:44:54,692
ABOUT NOT HAVING MORE CHILDREN.

850
00:44:54,822 --> 00:44:56,781
HAVING GIRLS
MUST BE SUCH FUN.

851
00:44:56,911 --> 00:44:59,087
BUT WE ALWAYS FELT
THAT HAVING AN ONLY CHILD

852
00:44:59,218 --> 00:45:02,308
WAS A MUCH BETTER WAY TO MOLD
AND SHAPE THEIR CHARACTER.

853
00:45:02,438 --> 00:45:04,658
Lydia: ASHLEY WAS ALONE
FOR HER FIRST SIX YEARS.

854
00:45:04,789 --> 00:45:07,443
I LIKE TO THINK SHE GOT
THE BEST OF BOTH WORLDS.

855
00:45:07,574 --> 00:45:10,229
Halley: MY BEST FRIEND
IS AN ONLY CHILD.

856
00:45:12,100 --> 00:45:13,885
SHE'S HAVING A BABY,

857
00:45:14,015 --> 00:45:15,625
WHICH I KNOW AT OUR AGE

858
00:45:15,756 --> 00:45:17,366
IS SOMETHING THAT
OBVIOUSLY WASN'T PLANNED.

859
00:45:17,497 --> 00:45:20,456
AND HER MOM IS NOT REALLY
THRILLED ABOUT THE SITUATION,

860
00:45:20,587 --> 00:45:22,458
BUT I REALLY THINK

861
00:45:22,589 --> 00:45:25,635
THAT SHE'S KIND OF STARTING
TO GET BEHIND IT RIGHT NOW.

862
00:45:25,766 --> 00:45:26,724
SO...

863
00:45:29,422 --> 00:45:30,597
OH!

864
00:45:37,647 --> 00:45:40,259
UM, WHICH WAY
TO THE BATHROOM?

865
00:45:40,389 --> 00:45:42,391
RIGHT DOWN THE HALL
AND TO YOUR LEFT.

866
00:46:05,110 --> 00:46:06,633
Mrs. Warsher:
ISN'T IT A SURPRISE--

867
00:46:06,764 --> 00:46:08,853
OUR CHILDREN CHOOSING
TO GET MARRIED SO YOUNG.

868
00:46:08,983 --> 00:46:10,898
I ALWAYS THOUGHT LEWIS
WOULD TAKE HIS TIME

869
00:46:11,029 --> 00:46:12,334
TO FIND THE RIGHT PERSON.

870
00:46:15,511 --> 00:46:18,384
Lewis: WELL, IT MUST BE
THE EXAMPLE OF YOU AND DAD.

871
00:46:18,514 --> 00:46:21,909
I MEAN... YOU MAKE MARRIAGE
SEEM SO FUN.

872
00:46:22,997 --> 00:46:25,957
AND ASHLEY'S A LOT
LIKE YOU, MOM.

873
00:46:30,004 --> 00:46:32,964
UH, SHE'S A VERY
DETERMINED WOMAN.

874
00:46:33,094 --> 00:46:35,401
[ smoke alarm beeps ]

875
00:46:38,665 --> 00:46:39,753
[ dog barking ]

876
00:46:39,884 --> 00:46:41,233
[ beeping ]

877
00:46:41,363 --> 00:46:42,887
All: HALLEY?

878
00:46:43,017 --> 00:46:44,192
[ knock on door ]

879
00:46:44,323 --> 00:46:46,281
Lydia:
OPEN THE DOOR, HALLEY.

880
00:46:46,412 --> 00:46:47,630
Mr. Warsher: YOUNG LADY?

881
00:46:47,761 --> 00:46:49,763
Lydia: OPEN THE DOOR.
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

882
00:47:01,993 --> 00:47:03,821
LOVELY EVENING.
THANK YOU.

883
00:47:07,520 --> 00:47:08,869
THANKS FOR STICKING UP FOR ME.

884
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:10,958
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

885
00:47:11,089 --> 00:47:14,832
YOUR MOM OBVIOUSLY DOESN'T
WANT YOU TO GET MARRIED.

886
00:47:14,962 --> 00:47:17,138
YOU MADE IT SOUND LIKE
I'M SOME DESPERATE WOMAN

887
00:47:17,269 --> 00:47:19,010
SOMEHOW FORCING YOU
INTO THE WHOLE THING.

888
00:47:19,140 --> 00:47:20,620
I DID NOT.

889
00:47:20,750 --> 00:47:22,665
"ASHLEY'S A VERY
DETERMINED WOMAN."

890
00:47:22,796 --> 00:47:23,971
OH, I DIDN'T SAY THAT.

891
00:47:24,102 --> 00:47:26,495
I HAVE WITNESSES!
MOM, YOU WERE THERE.

892
00:47:26,626 --> 00:47:28,280
YOU DID SAY SOMETHING
ALONG THOSE LINES.

893
00:47:28,410 --> 00:47:30,282
WELL, THAT IS NOT
HOW I MEANT IT.

894
00:47:30,412 --> 00:47:32,414
LEWIS, YOU HAVE
A LOVELY FAMILY

895
00:47:32,545 --> 00:47:33,938
AND THAT IS
WHAT IS IMPORTANT.

896
00:47:34,068 --> 00:47:36,331
THEY WEREN'T
EXACTLY LOVELY TO YOU.

897
00:47:36,462 --> 00:47:38,725
"OH, YOU ACTUALLY WORK
FOR A LIVING,

898
00:47:38,856 --> 00:47:41,815
YOU LOWER CLASS,
PATHETIC DIVORCéE?

899
00:47:41,946 --> 00:47:43,425
Lydia: ASHLEY, ENOUGH.

900
00:47:46,733 --> 00:47:49,388
I'M THE ONE WHO GOT
HUMPED BY A DOG IN THERE.

901
00:48:04,142 --> 00:48:06,622
[ soft tapping sound ]

902
00:48:29,515 --> 00:48:30,690
Halley: WHERE ARE WE?

903
00:48:30,820 --> 00:48:32,213
Macon: YOU'LL SEE
WHEN WE GET THERE.

904
00:48:32,344 --> 00:48:33,519
IT'S TOO DARK TO SEE.

905
00:48:33,649 --> 00:48:34,955
JUST HOLD ON.

906
00:49:17,693 --> 00:49:20,305
ME AND SHERWOOD FOUND
THIS PLACE A COUPLE YEARS AGO.

907
00:49:22,046 --> 00:49:23,351
WE USED TO COME HERE.

908
00:49:28,182 --> 00:49:29,531
[ music plays ]

909
00:49:29,662 --> 00:49:30,750
YOU LIKE IT?

910
00:49:30,880 --> 00:49:32,839
♪ A LITTLE SOMETHIN' SWEET

911
00:49:32,970 --> 00:49:34,928
YEAH.

912
00:49:35,059 --> 00:49:36,451
♪ LOVE CAN MAKE YOU

913
00:49:36,582 --> 00:49:37,539
COME ON,
LET'S DANCE.

914
00:49:37,670 --> 00:49:38,540
NO.

915
00:49:38,671 --> 00:49:39,541
YES.

916
00:49:39,672 --> 00:49:40,673
NO.YES.

917
00:49:40,803 --> 00:49:42,283
NOPE.

918
00:49:42,414 --> 00:49:44,242
♪ I SO WANT

919
00:49:44,372 --> 00:49:45,895
COME ON, MACON.

920
00:49:46,026 --> 00:49:46,896
NO.

921
00:49:47,027 --> 00:49:47,941
MACON!

922
00:49:48,072 --> 00:49:49,160
PLEASE?
COME ON, MACON.

923
00:49:49,290 --> 00:49:50,596
♪ A BOY
THAT'S SO STRONG ♪

924
00:49:50,726 --> 00:49:51,684
NO.

925
00:49:51,814 --> 00:49:53,033
♪ A LOVE THAT'S SO TRUE

926
00:49:53,164 --> 00:49:54,948
YOU LOOK GREAT,
BUT I JUST...

927
00:49:55,079 --> 00:49:59,257
♪ I THINK ABOUT HER,
THAT'S ALL I DO ♪

928
00:49:59,387 --> 00:50:01,389
[ siren blares ]

929
00:50:34,205 --> 00:50:36,729
MICHAEL'S PARENTS
MOVED TO FLORIDA.

930
00:50:36,859 --> 00:50:39,123
YOU STILL HAVE
TO TELL THEM.

931
00:50:39,253 --> 00:50:40,254
I KNOW.

932
00:50:41,995 --> 00:50:43,127
I JUST CAN'T FIGURE OUT

933
00:50:43,257 --> 00:50:45,912
WHAT TO SAY
THAT MAKES ANY SENSE.

934
00:50:46,043 --> 00:50:47,044
WHICH MAKES SENSE,

935
00:50:47,174 --> 00:50:48,480
GIVEN THAT NONE
OF WHAT'S HAPPENED

936
00:50:48,610 --> 00:50:49,655
MAKES ANY SENSE.

937
00:50:49,785 --> 00:50:51,396
[ laughs ]

938
00:50:51,526 --> 00:50:52,614
OH...

939
00:50:52,745 --> 00:50:55,226
YOU KNOW, IT'S WEIRD.

940
00:50:55,356 --> 00:50:59,273
BECAUSE IF YOU WERE
THE ONE THAT WAS PREGNANT,

941
00:50:59,404 --> 00:51:03,190
I WOULD UNDERSTAND YOU
CONSIDERING HAVING AN ABORTION

942
00:51:03,321 --> 00:51:07,020
OR PUTTING THE BABY
UP FOR ADOPTION.

943
00:51:08,848 --> 00:51:12,286
YOU CAN STILL PUT
THE BABY UP FOR ADOPTION.

944
00:51:12,417 --> 00:51:13,418
NO.

945
00:51:15,289 --> 00:51:16,943
I KNOW ALL THE ARGUMENTS.

946
00:51:19,119 --> 00:51:20,990
AND I KNOW
WHAT I'M GIVING UP.

947
00:51:24,777 --> 00:51:29,434
AND I KNOW THAT NOTHING IS
GONNA BE NORMAL FOR ME ANYMORE.

948
00:51:29,564 --> 00:51:31,088
[ chuckles ]

949
00:51:31,218 --> 00:51:34,091
OH, BUT WHAT
IS NORMAL, ANYWAY?

950
00:51:36,005 --> 00:51:38,312
GROWING UP WITH MY MOM
SURE WASN'T.

951
00:51:41,010 --> 00:51:42,708
LOSING MICHAEL WASN'T.

952
00:51:47,234 --> 00:51:48,844
I USED TO THINK
THAT MY FAMILY

953
00:51:48,975 --> 00:51:51,586
WAS THE PICTURE-PERFECT
EXAMPLE OF NORMAL.

954
00:51:52,761 --> 00:51:53,762
US.

955
00:51:56,069 --> 00:51:59,464
MAYBE BEING ABNORMAL
IS WHAT'S NORMAL, RIGHT?

956
00:51:59,594 --> 00:52:01,161
YEAH, IT'S LIKE
YOU AND MACON.

957
00:52:02,728 --> 00:52:03,859
IT DOESN'T MAKE ANY SENSE--

958
00:52:03,990 --> 00:52:06,427
YOU FALLING IN LOVE
WITH A GUY LIKE HIM.

959
00:52:06,558 --> 00:52:08,255
I'M NOT FALLING IN LOVE
WITH HIM,

960
00:52:08,386 --> 00:52:10,605
I LIKE KISSING HIM.

961
00:52:10,736 --> 00:52:12,738
WE'RE JUST FRIENDS.

962
00:52:12,868 --> 00:52:14,696
WITH BENEFITS.

963
00:52:14,827 --> 00:52:16,089
SHUT UP.

964
00:52:16,220 --> 00:52:17,743
BYE, I'M LEAVING.

965
00:52:17,873 --> 00:52:19,310
YOU'VE GOT IT BAD,
HALLEY!

966
00:52:19,440 --> 00:52:20,572
I'M LEAVING!

967
00:52:39,286 --> 00:52:41,245
I HOPE THIS ISN'T
A BAD TIME.

968
00:52:46,337 --> 00:52:48,904
I KNOW THIS IS AWFULLY
FORWARD OF ME,

969
00:52:49,035 --> 00:52:52,865
BUT I CAN'T STOP
THINKING ABOUT YOU.

970
00:53:04,442 --> 00:53:06,139
YOU'RE OUT OF UNIFORM.

971
00:53:06,270 --> 00:53:08,620
OH, THAT. I FORGOT
I WAS WEARING THAT.

972
00:53:08,750 --> 00:53:10,099
DIDN'T I EXPLAIN?

973
00:53:10,230 --> 00:53:13,233
I'M A CIVIL WAR REENACTOR--
A LITTLE HOBBY.

974
00:53:13,364 --> 00:53:15,322
I GUESS I LIKE
THINKING ABOUT A TIME

975
00:53:15,453 --> 00:53:18,586
WHEN HONOR AND CHIVALRY
REALLY MEANT SOMETHING.

976
00:53:18,717 --> 00:53:21,676
I KNOW I'VE BEEN SLOW
TO TAKE ACTION.

977
00:53:21,807 --> 00:53:23,200
SLOW'S GOOD.

978
00:53:23,330 --> 00:53:25,419
WOULD DINNER TONIGHT
BE TOO FAST?

979
00:53:25,550 --> 00:53:26,855
YES.

980
00:53:28,205 --> 00:53:30,207
I MEAN, NO.
I MEAN, I'D LOVE TO.

981
00:53:31,251 --> 00:53:36,865
♪ LONG AGO

982
00:53:36,996 --> 00:53:40,782
♪ I DREW A LINE
INTO THE SAND ♪

983
00:53:40,913 --> 00:53:43,742
♪ JUMPED ACROSS
AND HELD YOUR HAND ♪

984
00:53:43,872 --> 00:53:45,526
♪ BAND OF GOLD

985
00:53:45,657 --> 00:53:46,832
CHEERS.

986
00:53:50,183 --> 00:53:53,360
♪ PROTECT US
FROM THE BITTER TIDE ♪

987
00:53:53,491 --> 00:53:58,147
♪ THAT COMES TO WASH AWAY
OUR WORDS WITH TIME ♪

988
00:53:58,278 --> 00:54:01,673
♪ HELLO, YOU

989
00:54:01,803 --> 00:54:05,111
♪ HELLO, ME

990
00:54:05,242 --> 00:54:07,896
♪ HELLO, HELLO

991
00:54:08,027 --> 00:54:10,856
♪ CAN'T YOU SEE

992
00:54:10,986 --> 00:54:18,559
♪ LOVE IS
MORE THAN WHAT IT SEEMS? ♪

993
00:54:18,690 --> 00:54:20,518
FRIENDS?

994
00:54:20,648 --> 00:54:22,259
FRIENDS.

995
00:54:25,566 --> 00:54:27,960
STEVE, I HAD A LOVELY TIME.

996
00:54:35,141 --> 00:54:40,189
♪ PROMISES

997
00:54:40,320 --> 00:54:41,495
GOOD NIGHT.

998
00:54:41,626 --> 00:54:44,672
♪ MADE UNDER
THE RITE OF SPRING ♪

999
00:54:44,803 --> 00:54:47,719
♪ HEAVY UNDER SUMMER'S SCENE

1000
00:54:47,849 --> 00:54:48,894
OH!

1001
00:54:50,722 --> 00:54:51,766
I-I-I WAS JUST--

1002
00:54:51,897 --> 00:54:53,072
YOU WERE JUST LEAVING.

1003
00:54:53,202 --> 00:54:54,508
EXACTLY.

1004
00:54:55,770 --> 00:54:56,771
HALLEY.

1005
00:54:59,078 --> 00:55:01,428
THIS IS HOW YOU CONDUCT
YOURSELF IN YOUR OWN HOME?

1006
00:55:01,559 --> 00:55:03,082
YOU SAID IT--
MY OWN HOME.

1007
00:55:03,212 --> 00:55:05,737
THAT IMPLIES I HAVE A RIGHT
TO CHOOSE WHAT I DO!

1008
00:55:05,867 --> 00:55:08,217
HALLEY MARIE MARTIN,
CONDUCT UNBECOMING.

1009
00:55:08,348 --> 00:55:09,349
[ knock on door ]

1010
00:55:09,480 --> 00:55:10,307
NO!

1011
00:55:10,437 --> 00:55:11,308
[ louder knock ]

1012
00:55:11,438 --> 00:55:12,918
NO!

1013
00:55:16,051 --> 00:55:18,880
YOU NEVER TOLD ME YOU WERE
SERIOUS ABOUT THIS BOY.

1014
00:55:19,011 --> 00:55:20,534
I'M NOT SERIOUS.

1015
00:55:20,665 --> 00:55:22,667
THAT'S WHAT YOU DO WITH PEOPLE
YOU'RE NOT SERIOUS ABOUT?

1016
00:55:22,797 --> 00:55:23,842
YOU KNOW WHAT?

1017
00:55:23,972 --> 00:55:25,931
MAYBE IF YOU HAD
A LITTLE BIT MORE FUN,

1018
00:55:26,061 --> 00:55:28,542
YOU WOULDN'T BE IN THE POSITION
YOU'RE IN RIGHT NOW.

1019
00:55:28,673 --> 00:55:30,805
WHERE IS ALL THIS ATTITUDE
COMING FROM, HALLEY?

1020
00:55:30,936 --> 00:55:32,111
THIS IS NOT LIKE YOU.

1021
00:55:32,241 --> 00:55:33,242
LIKE ME?

1022
00:55:33,373 --> 00:55:34,766
MOM, YOU DON'T
EVEN KNOW ME.

1023
00:55:34,896 --> 00:55:36,681
MAYBE YOU'RE NOT VERY GOOD
AT KNOWING PEOPLE.

1024
00:55:36,811 --> 00:55:38,683
HOW WELL DO YOU KNOW
THAT STRANGE BOY?

1025
00:55:38,813 --> 00:55:40,424
MOM, HE'S NOT
STRANGE, OKAY?

1026
00:55:40,554 --> 00:55:41,903
HIS NAME IS MACON.

1027
00:55:42,034 --> 00:55:44,079
AND MAYBE IF YOU PAID
ATTENTION TO ANYONE--

1028
00:55:44,210 --> 00:55:46,212
GOD FORBID--
BESIDES YOURSELF

1029
00:55:46,343 --> 00:55:48,170
AND ASHLEY
AND HER STUPID WEDDING,

1030
00:55:48,301 --> 00:55:49,781
YOU WOULD KNOW THAT.

1031
00:56:04,883 --> 00:56:06,188
I'M TRYING.

1032
00:56:08,713 --> 00:56:11,977
HALLEY,
YOU USED TO TALK TO ME.

1033
00:56:12,107 --> 00:56:15,720
YEAH, AND YOU WERE TOO BUSY
HATING DAD TO LISTEN.

1034
00:56:26,165 --> 00:56:28,602
I'M SORRY YOU'VE HAD
TO GO THROUGH THIS. I'M...

1035
00:56:33,259 --> 00:56:36,567
I HATE DAD...

1036
00:56:36,697 --> 00:56:38,656
SO MUCH
FOR DOING THIS TO US.

1037
00:56:40,832 --> 00:56:42,703
I HATE HIM, I HATE HIM.

1038
00:56:46,141 --> 00:56:47,665
AND THEN
I DON'T HATE HIM,

1039
00:56:47,795 --> 00:56:49,493
AND I FEEL BAD
FOR HATING HIM.

1040
00:56:49,623 --> 00:56:51,973
SWEETIE, I DON'T WANT YOU
TO HATE YOUR FATHER.

1041
00:56:52,104 --> 00:56:53,758
HE'S A DECENT MAN.

1042
00:56:58,371 --> 00:57:00,199
I DON'T WANT YOU
TO HATE ME, EITHER,

1043
00:57:00,329 --> 00:57:03,071
BUT I AM GOING TO HAVE TO START
LAYING DOWN SOME RULES.

1044
00:57:03,202 --> 00:57:04,333
OH, HERE WE GO.

1045
00:57:04,464 --> 00:57:06,858
HALLEY, YOU'RE GROUNDED
UNTIL NEXT YEAR.

1046
00:57:06,988 --> 00:57:08,512
NO. NO, NO, NO.

1047
00:57:08,642 --> 00:57:10,731
YOU PROMISED ME
THAT I COULD GO

1048
00:57:10,862 --> 00:57:13,995
TO THE NEW YEAR'S EVE PARTY
WITH MACON--MOM, PLEASE!

1049
00:57:14,126 --> 00:57:17,434
NO. NO BUTS,
NO NEW YEAR'S EVE, NO MACON.

1050
00:57:19,610 --> 00:57:20,567
GOD!

1051
00:57:22,221 --> 00:57:25,224
[ music plays ]

1052
00:57:30,969 --> 00:57:33,841
"DEAR MR.
AND MRS. SHERWOOD...

1053
00:57:33,972 --> 00:57:36,888
"GUESS WHAT? YOU'RE
GONNA BE GRANDPARENTS--"

1054
00:57:37,018 --> 00:57:38,367
EXCLAMATION POINT.

1055
00:57:43,590 --> 00:57:45,244
WHY DON'T YOU TRY TELLING
MICHAEL'S PARENTS

1056
00:57:45,374 --> 00:57:46,680
WHAT YOU REALLY FEEL?

1057
00:57:48,073 --> 00:57:51,468
[ cell phone rings ]

1058
00:57:58,518 --> 00:57:59,650
MACON LAND.

1059
00:58:02,261 --> 00:58:03,915
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

1060
00:58:06,787 --> 00:58:08,267
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

1061
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:16,188
♪♪

1062
00:58:23,935 --> 00:58:27,460
♪ NO ONE LIKES TO LEAVE

1063
00:58:27,591 --> 00:58:28,940
♪ YEAH

1064
00:58:29,070 --> 00:58:32,204
♪ LEAVIN', LEAVIN', YEAH

1065
00:58:32,334 --> 00:58:36,077
♪ NO ONE LIKES TO LEAVE

1066
00:58:36,208 --> 00:58:37,644
♪ YEAH

1067
00:58:37,775 --> 00:58:40,908
♪ LEAVIN', LEAVIN', YEAH

1068
00:58:41,039 --> 00:58:44,738
♪ SHE'S COMPLETELY FREE

1069
00:58:54,226 --> 00:58:56,620
HEY, MACON, THE MAN.

1070
00:58:56,750 --> 00:58:57,795
HI.

1071
00:58:57,925 --> 00:58:59,100
[ laughs ]

1072
00:58:59,231 --> 00:59:00,798
THE PARTY'S JUST ARRIVED.

1073
00:59:00,928 --> 00:59:02,495
THE PARTY HAS--
I'M HERE.

1074
00:59:04,628 --> 00:59:07,195
[ rap music plays ]

1075
00:59:07,326 --> 00:59:08,196
YEAH.

1076
00:59:08,327 --> 00:59:09,328
OKAY.

1077
00:59:11,417 --> 00:59:12,418
SORRY.

1078
00:59:22,080 --> 00:59:24,256
NOW, YOUARE PRETTY.

1079
00:59:25,953 --> 00:59:27,085
AW...

1080
00:59:29,261 --> 00:59:31,655
COME ON, YOU CAN SMILE
BETTER THAN THAT.

1081
00:59:32,960 --> 00:59:34,135
Macon: HEY!

1082
00:59:34,266 --> 00:59:35,746
WHAT? SHE DOESN'T KNOW
HOW TO SMILE?

1083
00:59:35,876 --> 00:59:37,443
MAYBE SHE DOESN'T WANT TO.

1084
00:59:37,574 --> 00:59:39,401
WELL, EXCUSE ME
FOR BREATHING.

1085
00:59:39,532 --> 00:59:41,795
YEAH, YOU'RE BREATHING
TOO CLOSE.

1086
00:59:41,926 --> 00:59:42,796
SORRY ABOUT THIS.

1087
00:59:42,927 --> 00:59:43,884
IT'S OKAY.

1088
00:59:45,625 --> 00:59:46,495
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

1089
00:59:46,626 --> 00:59:47,758
HAPPY NEW YEAR.

1090
00:59:49,803 --> 00:59:51,805
HERE'S TO THE NEW YEAR,
RIGHT?

1091
00:59:51,936 --> 00:59:55,809
YEAH, RIGHT.
TO THE NEW YEAR. WHOO.

1092
00:59:55,940 --> 00:59:58,029
OKAY, KNOCK-KNOCK.
POLICE RAID.

1093
01:00:00,640 --> 01:00:04,035
HEY, MACON, MY MAN...
WHAT'S UP?

1094
01:00:04,165 --> 01:00:05,602
WHAT'S UP WITH YOU?

1095
01:00:08,126 --> 01:00:09,431
I LOST MY DAMN EARRING.

1096
01:00:10,650 --> 01:00:11,608
HEY, MACON.

1097
01:00:14,001 --> 01:00:14,959
HI, HALLEY.

1098
01:00:16,438 --> 01:00:17,439
HI.

1099
01:00:18,440 --> 01:00:19,441
THANKS.

1100
01:00:23,532 --> 01:00:24,882
Boy: HALLEY...

1101
01:00:25,012 --> 01:00:26,100
NICE NAME.

1102
01:00:28,537 --> 01:00:31,932
HEY! WHO WANTS
TO SEE MY FERRET?

1103
01:00:33,107 --> 01:00:34,935
DUDE, I HAVE ONE.
I HAVE ONE.

1104
01:00:35,066 --> 01:00:37,068
COME ON, DUDE.

1105
01:00:37,198 --> 01:00:39,200
I PUT A LITTLE HAT ON HIM
AND EVERYTHING.

1106
01:00:39,331 --> 01:00:40,811
IT'S AWESOME.

1107
01:00:52,997 --> 01:00:56,000
SO, WHEN'S
SCARLETT DUE, ANYWAY?

1108
01:01:00,047 --> 01:01:01,614
YOU KNOW?

1109
01:01:01,745 --> 01:01:04,051
YEAH, MY MOM'S A BOOKKEEPER
IN HER DOCTOR'S OFFICE.

1110
01:01:04,182 --> 01:01:07,054
BUT...DON'T WORRY.
I HAVEN'T TOLD ANYONE.

1111
01:01:08,273 --> 01:01:10,492
THIRD WEEK OF MAY.

1112
01:01:10,623 --> 01:01:13,017
GOD, THAT IS SO FREAKY.

1113
01:01:15,019 --> 01:01:16,716
YOU KNOW, IT'S WEIRD, BUT...

1114
01:01:16,847 --> 01:01:18,892
I DIDN'T EVEN KNOW
THEY'D HOOKED UP.

1115
01:01:19,023 --> 01:01:22,461
REALLY? 'CAUSE THEY
WENT OUT ALL SUMMER.

1116
01:01:22,591 --> 01:01:23,810
DID THEY?

1117
01:01:23,941 --> 01:01:26,465
YEAH, AND HE WAS
COMPLETELY IN LOVE WITH HER.

1118
01:01:26,595 --> 01:01:27,945
SHE'S RUINING HER LIFE,
YOU KNOW.

1119
01:01:28,075 --> 01:01:30,469
I THINK I'D KILL MYSELF
BEFORE I HAD A BABY.

1120
01:01:30,599 --> 01:01:31,905
I KNOW ENOUGH

1121
01:01:32,036 --> 01:01:34,691
TO KNOW I WOULDN'T
BE ABLE TO HANDLE IT.

1122
01:01:34,821 --> 01:01:37,737
YOU'RE PROBABLY RIGHT,
BECAUSE YOU'RE NOT SCARLETT.

1123
01:01:37,868 --> 01:01:40,174
RIGHT.

1124
01:01:40,305 --> 01:01:41,698
THANK GOD FOR THAT.

1125
01:02:00,064 --> 01:02:03,981
♪ SUPPOSE I SAID

1126
01:02:04,111 --> 01:02:10,552
♪ I'M ON MY BEST BEHAVIOR

1127
01:02:10,683 --> 01:02:14,600
♪ THERE ARE TIMES

1128
01:02:14,731 --> 01:02:19,736
♪ I LOSE MY WORRIED MIND

1129
01:02:19,866 --> 01:02:22,434
♪ WOULD YOU WANT ME

1130
01:02:22,564 --> 01:02:26,917
♪ WHEN I'M NOT MYSELF?

1131
01:02:30,616 --> 01:02:32,618
♪ WAIT IT OUT

1132
01:02:32,749 --> 01:02:36,927
♪ WHILE I AM
SOMEONE ELSE? ♪

1133
01:02:42,759 --> 01:02:46,371
♪ SUPPOSE I SAID

1134
01:02:46,501 --> 01:02:51,245
♪ COLORS CHANGE
FOR NO GOOD REASON ♪

1135
01:02:53,639 --> 01:02:57,164
♪ WORDS WILL GO

1136
01:02:57,295 --> 01:03:02,474
♪ FROM POETRY TO PROSE

1137
01:03:02,604 --> 01:03:05,129
♪ WOULD YOU WANT ME

1138
01:03:05,259 --> 01:03:09,829
♪ WHEN I'M NOT MYSELF?

1139
01:03:13,354 --> 01:03:15,182
♪ WAIT IT OUT

1140
01:03:15,313 --> 01:03:19,665
♪ WHILE I AM SOMEONE ELSE?

1141
01:03:23,321 --> 01:03:25,802
♪ AND I

1142
01:03:29,022 --> 01:03:31,111
♪ IN TIME

1143
01:03:31,242 --> 01:03:32,721
WHAT'S WRONG?

1144
01:03:34,158 --> 01:03:36,813
♪ WILL COME AROUND

1145
01:03:36,943 --> 01:03:38,075
I'M SORRY.

1146
01:03:38,205 --> 01:03:41,600
♪ I ALWAYS DO

1147
01:03:41,730 --> 01:03:43,558
HALLEY, WHERE ARE YOU GOING?

1148
01:03:43,689 --> 01:03:46,997
♪ FOR YOU

1149
01:03:49,651 --> 01:03:52,002
[ talking and laughing ]

1150
01:03:58,486 --> 01:04:02,403
All: TEN, NINE, EIGHT, SEVEN,

1151
01:04:02,534 --> 01:04:05,667
SIX, FIVE, FOUR,

1152
01:04:05,798 --> 01:04:08,932
THREE, TWO, ONE.

1153
01:04:09,062 --> 01:04:11,195
[ cheering ]

1154
01:04:32,346 --> 01:04:33,695
I'M SORRY.

1155
01:04:39,571 --> 01:04:41,051
I REALLY AM.

1156
01:04:46,186 --> 01:04:47,666
WHAT WAS THAT ALL ABOUT?

1157
01:04:51,104 --> 01:04:53,802
I THOUGHT YOU WANTED US
TO BE TOGETHER.

1158
01:04:55,674 --> 01:04:58,807
I--I DO--
BUT, "TOGETHER"?

1159
01:05:00,418 --> 01:05:06,206
IT'S SO OFFICIAL
AND SO BIG FOR--FOR US.

1160
01:05:06,337 --> 01:05:09,253
MAYBE YOU SHOULD JUST SAY
WHAT YOU FEEL FOR ONCE, HUH?

1161
01:05:10,950 --> 01:05:12,256
I COULD DO THAT.

1162
01:05:14,432 --> 01:05:15,433
I CAN.

1163
01:05:16,782 --> 01:05:17,914
I CAN.

1164
01:05:21,352 --> 01:05:24,616
I FELT LIKE I HAD TO GET
OUT OF THERE BECAUSE I MIGHT...

1165
01:05:27,358 --> 01:05:28,881
REALLY...

1166
01:05:31,362 --> 01:05:33,625
CARE ABOUT YOU, AND...

1167
01:05:37,107 --> 01:05:41,589
AND IT SCARED ME SO MUCH
BECAUSE THAT MEANT THAT...

1168
01:05:41,720 --> 01:05:43,461
YOU COULD HURT ME.

1169
01:05:45,680 --> 01:05:48,814
OR MAYBE I
JUST DIDN'T FEEL READY...

1170
01:05:52,470 --> 01:05:54,776
TO LIKE SOMEONE...
THAT MUCH.

1171
01:05:57,562 --> 01:05:58,737
AND I LIKE YOU.

1172
01:06:01,218 --> 01:06:03,394
DON'T MAKE IT
SO COMPLICATED, HALLEY.

1173
01:06:06,179 --> 01:06:07,224
[ horn honking ]

1174
01:06:07,354 --> 01:06:08,965
[ screams ]

1175
01:06:11,445 --> 01:06:14,057
[ horn honks ]

1176
01:06:56,360 --> 01:06:59,537
SOME PEOPLE FALL IN LOVE.

1177
01:06:59,667 --> 01:07:01,843
I HAD TO CRASH INTO IT.

1178
01:07:20,688 --> 01:07:22,255
HEY, BABY.

1179
01:07:22,386 --> 01:07:23,387
HI.

1180
01:07:25,084 --> 01:07:26,999
I'M SORRY.

1181
01:07:27,130 --> 01:07:29,045
YOU GAVE US QUITE A SCARE.

1182
01:07:31,090 --> 01:07:33,136
GOD.

1183
01:07:33,266 --> 01:07:35,051
AND I RUINED YOUR PARTY, TOO.

1184
01:07:36,313 --> 01:07:38,184
I'M NOT CONCERNED
WITH THE PARTY.

1185
01:07:38,315 --> 01:07:39,403
YOUR DATE WITH STEVE.

1186
01:07:39,533 --> 01:07:41,492
I KNOW THAT WAS
SO IMPORTANT TO YOU.

1187
01:07:41,622 --> 01:07:44,408
HALLEY, I KNOW YOU WERE
WITH MACON FORRESTER.

1188
01:07:46,627 --> 01:07:48,194
MOM, IT WAS NOT
HIS FAULT, THOUGH.

1189
01:07:48,325 --> 01:07:50,718
WE WERE TRYING TO LEAVE
THIS BAD PARTY AND GET HOME.

1190
01:07:50,849 --> 01:07:52,155
HE WAS LETTING ME DRIVE--

1191
01:07:52,285 --> 01:07:54,896
YOU GUYS KNOW I'M
THE WORSE DRIVER IN THE WORLD.

1192
01:07:55,027 --> 01:07:56,507
AND I COULD NOT EVEN SEE--

1193
01:07:56,637 --> 01:07:58,335
HALLEY, SAVE YOUR STRENGTH.

1194
01:07:58,465 --> 01:08:00,772
YOU'RE GONNA NEED IT TO COME
UP WITH BETTER EXCUSES.

1195
01:08:11,261 --> 01:08:16,614
♪ THINKIN' ABOUT TOMORROW

1196
01:08:16,744 --> 01:08:22,141
♪ TIRED FROM ALL THE TIME
I SPENT ♪

1197
01:08:22,272 --> 01:08:24,883
MACON WASN'T THERE
WHEN I WOKE UP.

1198
01:08:25,013 --> 01:08:29,061
MACON WASN'T THERE
WHEN I LEFT.

1199
01:08:29,192 --> 01:08:34,284
MACON WASN'T THERE
THE WHOLE NEXT WEEK AT SCHOOL.

1200
01:08:34,414 --> 01:08:37,069
WHAT DO YOU EXPECT
WHEN YOU BREAK YOUR OWN RULES?

1201
01:08:40,725 --> 01:08:41,856
ANY WORD FROM HIM?

1202
01:08:41,987 --> 01:08:42,988
NO.

1203
01:08:46,818 --> 01:08:49,125
I GUESS THAT'S WHAT GUYS
ARE GOOD AT, RIGHT?

1204
01:08:50,691 --> 01:08:52,040
DISAPPEARING?

1205
01:08:54,695 --> 01:08:59,396
♪ SO LONG

1206
01:08:59,526 --> 01:09:05,402
♪ BYE, MY FRIENDS,
SO LONG ♪

1207
01:09:05,532 --> 01:09:06,751
♪ SO LONG

1208
01:09:06,881 --> 01:09:15,412
♪ WILL IT EVER
HAPPEN AGAIN? ♪

1209
01:09:15,542 --> 01:09:17,675
HEY. I'M BACK.

1210
01:09:23,811 --> 01:09:25,552
YOU REALLY DON'T GET IT,
DO YOU?

1211
01:09:29,121 --> 01:09:32,255
AND I'M REALLY NOT IN THE MOOD
TO WAIT FOR YOU TO GROW UP.

1212
01:10:16,690 --> 01:10:17,865
MACON?

1213
01:10:24,263 --> 01:10:25,917
ASHLEY?

1214
01:10:26,047 --> 01:10:29,050
OH, MY GOD,
ARE YOU OKAY?

1215
01:10:31,096 --> 01:10:32,402
HI, HALLEY.

1216
01:10:34,186 --> 01:10:36,144
I THINK
I JUST DROPPED MY KEYS.

1217
01:10:36,275 --> 01:10:38,843
NO, THEY'RE IN THE DOOR.
COME ON. OW!

1218
01:10:38,973 --> 01:10:42,063
HI. STOP SPINNING!
STOP SPINNING, STOP SPINNING.

1219
01:10:42,194 --> 01:10:43,630
I'M NOT SPINNING!

1220
01:10:43,761 --> 01:10:45,502
SHH!

1221
01:10:45,632 --> 01:10:46,764
[ whispers ]
Quiet!

1222
01:10:49,593 --> 01:10:51,986
MAYBE YOUSHOULD BE QUIET.

1223
01:10:52,117 --> 01:10:53,466
THAT'S WHAT YOU SHOULD DO.

1224
01:10:53,597 --> 01:10:55,381
Ashley.
Ashley, upstairs.

1225
01:10:55,512 --> 01:10:57,514
OH, HALLEY,
YOU'RE SUCH A GOOD SISTER.

1226
01:10:57,644 --> 01:10:59,255
Shh!

1227
01:10:59,385 --> 01:11:02,736
WHOA...YOU THINK
I'M DOING THOSE?

1228
01:11:02,867 --> 01:11:04,172
I AM NOT
DOING THOSE.

1229
01:11:04,303 --> 01:11:05,739
Be careful. Shh!

1230
01:11:05,870 --> 01:11:08,742
CHRIST, HALLEY.
IT'S ALL RIGHT!

1231
01:11:10,178 --> 01:11:14,444
THIS IS MY BACHELORETTE PARTY!

1232
01:11:14,574 --> 01:11:16,576
I'M A BACHELORETTE!

1233
01:11:16,707 --> 01:11:18,056
WHOA!

1234
01:11:28,806 --> 01:11:30,155
OH...

1235
01:11:30,286 --> 01:11:33,941
THANK YOU, LITTLE SISTER.

1236
01:11:34,072 --> 01:11:35,769
YOU ARE THE GREATEST.

1237
01:11:35,900 --> 01:11:37,510
OKAY, ASHLEY--
ASHLEY!

1238
01:11:37,641 --> 01:11:39,730
PLEASE, JUST TAKE THIS.

1239
01:11:39,860 --> 01:11:40,948
JESUS. WHAT--

1240
01:11:41,079 --> 01:11:42,254
WHOA.

1241
01:11:43,821 --> 01:11:44,996
YOU JUST...

1242
01:11:45,126 --> 01:11:45,997
[ laughs ]

1243
01:11:46,127 --> 01:11:47,041
ASHLEY,

1244
01:11:47,172 --> 01:11:48,434
PLEASE. COME ON.

1245
01:11:48,565 --> 01:11:50,741
[ whispers ]
Mom is upstairs sleeping.

1246
01:11:50,871 --> 01:11:52,177
MOM'S NOT HOME.

1247
01:11:53,657 --> 01:11:56,921
OH, REALLY? AND HOW
WOULD YOU KNOW THAT?

1248
01:11:57,051 --> 01:12:01,055
FRIDAY NIGHTS SHE SNEAKS OUT
TO HAVE SEX WITH STEVE.

1249
01:12:01,186 --> 01:12:03,841
[ laughing ]

1250
01:12:09,194 --> 01:12:11,370
SHE TOLD YOU THAT?

1251
01:12:11,501 --> 01:12:13,764
SHE DIDN'T WANT
YOU TO KNOW.

1252
01:12:13,894 --> 01:12:17,594
GOD, WHY DO PEOPLE THINK
THAT I CAN'T HANDLE THE TRUTH?

1253
01:12:21,467 --> 01:12:22,947
Ashley...

1254
01:12:27,255 --> 01:12:29,432
YOU HATCHET-FACED SCARECROW.

1255
01:12:29,562 --> 01:12:30,781
YOU BABOON.

1256
01:12:30,911 --> 01:12:31,825
BAG OF BONES.

1257
01:12:31,956 --> 01:12:33,392
YOU SOUR PUSS.

1258
01:12:33,523 --> 01:12:35,176
[ knock on door ]

1259
01:12:37,178 --> 01:12:38,658
TOP OF THE MORNING TO YOU.

1260
01:12:38,789 --> 01:12:40,399
OOH...HOW IS SHE?

1261
01:12:41,618 --> 01:12:43,271
[ blows raspberry ]

1262
01:12:44,838 --> 01:12:45,970
SWEETIE.

1263
01:12:54,761 --> 01:12:55,588
A HANGOVER KIT.

1264
01:12:55,719 --> 01:12:57,111
OH...

1265
01:12:57,242 --> 01:12:59,766
NOT TO APPEAR SUPERIOR,
BUT I DID LIMIT MYSELF

1266
01:12:59,897 --> 01:13:02,421
TO ONE GLASS OF CHAMPAGNE,
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

1267
01:13:02,552 --> 01:13:05,250
IF IT WASN'T FOR HALLEY,
I WOULD'VE DIED, PROBABLY.

1268
01:13:05,381 --> 01:13:07,818
NO, YOU JUST WOULD'VE
WOKEN UP ON THE PORCH.

1269
01:13:07,948 --> 01:13:10,603
Lewis: I BET THE NEIGHBORS
WOULD'VE LOVED THAT.

1270
01:13:10,734 --> 01:13:12,779
RIGHT, ESPECIALLY
WITH THE, UH,

1271
01:13:12,910 --> 01:13:15,391
MEN'S UNDERWEAR
AROUND HER NECK.

1272
01:13:17,131 --> 01:13:18,306
UNDERWEAR?

1273
01:13:19,917 --> 01:13:21,484
IT WAS NOTHING.
JUST SOMETHING STUPID.

1274
01:13:21,614 --> 01:13:23,921
UNDERWEAR IS NOT "NOTHING."

1275
01:13:24,051 --> 01:13:27,577
UH, NO, THEY WERE
PRETTY MUCH NOTHING.

1276
01:13:30,536 --> 01:13:32,495
WE PROMISED EACH OTHER
NO STRIPPERS.

1277
01:13:32,625 --> 01:13:34,148
I KNOW, LEWIS.
I KNOW, I KNOW.

1278
01:13:34,279 --> 01:13:36,368
BUT I WAS AT THE MERCY
OF MY FRIENDS.

1279
01:13:36,499 --> 01:13:38,675
DON'T PROMISES WE MAKE
TO EACH OTHER MEAN ANYTHING?

1280
01:13:38,805 --> 01:13:41,286
YES, OF COURSE THEY MEAN
SOMETHING, LEWIS!

1281
01:13:41,417 --> 01:13:42,809
GOD, DON'T BE SO UPTIGHT!

1282
01:13:42,940 --> 01:13:44,768
OH, I'M UPTIGHT?
I-I-I--

1283
01:13:44,898 --> 01:13:47,640
YES, LEWIS, YOU ARE.
YOU ARE UPTIGHT.

1284
01:13:47,771 --> 01:13:50,077
AND YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE?
HALLEY WAS RIGHT ABOUT YOU.

1285
01:13:50,208 --> 01:13:52,428
YOU HAVE GOT
A BROOMSTICK UP YOUR BUTT.

1286
01:13:52,558 --> 01:13:53,864
I NEVER SAID THAT!

1287
01:13:53,994 --> 01:13:55,866
Lewis: WELL, GUESS
WHO PUT IT THERE?

1288
01:13:55,996 --> 01:13:58,434
DON'T TALK TO ME THAT WAY.
MAYBE I'LL FIND SOMEBODY FUN!

1289
01:13:58,564 --> 01:14:00,348
TO TELL THE TRUTH,
YOU ARE NO FUN!

1290
01:14:00,479 --> 01:14:02,089
WE MADE A PROMISE
TO EACH OTHER,

1291
01:14:02,220 --> 01:14:05,092
BUT YOU DON'T KEEP IT BECAUSE
YOU'RE TOO SELF-ABSORBED.

1292
01:14:05,223 --> 01:14:06,485
DON'T TALK TO ME THAT WAY.

1293
01:14:06,616 --> 01:14:08,487
Lydia: HELLO.
GOOD MORNING, HALLEY.

1294
01:14:08,618 --> 01:14:10,924
WHAT'S GOING ON
IN THERE?

1295
01:14:11,055 --> 01:14:12,143
I THINK
THEY'RE BREAKING UP.

1296
01:14:12,273 --> 01:14:13,797
Ashley: RELAX. YOU'RE NO FUN.

1297
01:14:13,927 --> 01:14:16,408
Lewis: MARRIAGE IS A PROMISE--
SOMETHING THAT HAS TO BE KEPT.

1298
01:14:16,539 --> 01:14:18,845
NOT EVERY ARGUMENT
LEADS TO A BREAKUP.

1299
01:14:18,976 --> 01:14:19,977
[ door opens ]

1300
01:14:20,107 --> 01:14:21,021
FOR REAL!

1301
01:14:21,152 --> 01:14:22,458
[ door slams ]

1302
01:14:25,548 --> 01:14:26,984
THE WEDDING IS OFF.

1303
01:14:31,510 --> 01:14:32,468
[ ring clatters ]

1304
01:14:41,912 --> 01:14:43,391
[ soft tapping sound ]

1305
01:15:06,850 --> 01:15:08,591
I'VE BEEN TRYING TO SAY
I'M SORRY.

1306
01:15:08,721 --> 01:15:11,724
"I'M SORRY" DOESN'T ALWAYS
CUT IT, MACON. GOD!

1307
01:15:16,033 --> 01:15:18,209
I COULDN'T STAY WITH YOU
AT THE HOSPITAL.

1308
01:15:18,339 --> 01:15:19,515
I KNOW I SHOULD HAVE,

1309
01:15:19,645 --> 01:15:21,517
BUT THINK HOW MUCH
MORE FREAKED OUT

1310
01:15:21,647 --> 01:15:23,954
YOUR MOM WOULD'VE GOT
IF SHE'D HAVE SEEN ME.

1311
01:15:27,044 --> 01:15:29,002
OH, MY GOD.

1312
01:15:29,133 --> 01:15:31,788
OKAY. WOW,
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

1313
01:15:31,918 --> 01:15:34,660
SO, YOU WERE DITCHING ME
FOR MY OWN BENEFIT?

1314
01:15:34,791 --> 01:15:35,748
AW...

1315
01:15:37,576 --> 01:15:39,839
NO, THAT'S NOT IT.

1316
01:15:39,970 --> 01:15:42,102
I--I DIDN'T DITCH YOU.

1317
01:15:43,800 --> 01:15:45,279
I...

1318
01:15:46,933 --> 01:15:48,544
OKAY, I...

1319
01:15:50,502 --> 01:15:51,851
I FREAKED OUT.

1320
01:15:53,549 --> 01:15:56,682
I'M NOT USED TO FEELING
THIS WAY ABOUT SOMEBODY.

1321
01:15:56,813 --> 01:15:58,945
AND I JUST...

1322
01:15:59,076 --> 01:16:01,382
I COULDN'T BELIEVE
I ALMOST LOST YOU, TOO.

1323
01:16:09,042 --> 01:16:10,261
HERE.

1324
01:16:10,391 --> 01:16:12,045
COME ON,
I'LL HELP YOU EAT THEM.

1325
01:16:13,177 --> 01:16:16,049
NO. I DON'T WANT ANY.

1326
01:16:20,184 --> 01:16:21,751
I CAN'T SEE YOU ANYMORE.

1327
01:16:24,797 --> 01:16:26,538
YOUR MOM WILL GET OVER IT.

1328
01:16:26,669 --> 01:16:28,758
IT'S NOT MY MOM. IT'S ME.

1329
01:16:31,761 --> 01:16:34,372
AND, OF COURSE, IF YOU DO
DECIDE TO GET MARRIED,

1330
01:16:34,502 --> 01:16:36,243
I CAN GET MY MAKEUP
AND HAIR PEOPLE

1331
01:16:36,374 --> 01:16:38,332
TO DO YOU
ON THE BIG DAY.

1332
01:16:38,463 --> 01:16:40,726
AND IF YOU DECIDE
NOT TO GET MARRIED,

1333
01:16:40,857 --> 01:16:43,686
I THINK YOU SHOULD LET THEM
DO SOME WORK ON YOU ANYWAY,

1334
01:16:43,816 --> 01:16:46,645
BECAUSE YOU ARE GONNA WANT
TO LOOK YOUR BEST

1335
01:16:46,776 --> 01:16:48,604
WHEN YOU GET BACK OUT THERE.

1336
01:16:52,172 --> 01:16:55,611
DARLING, THERE IS NOTHING WRONG
WITH CANCELING A WEDDING.

1337
01:16:55,741 --> 01:16:57,917
NO, IT'S INDEFINITELY POSTPONED.

1338
01:16:58,048 --> 01:17:00,790
THAT'S WHAT WE'RE SUPPOSED
TO SAY OFFICIALLY.

1339
01:17:00,920 --> 01:17:02,313
MY MOM FOUND OUT.

1340
01:17:02,443 --> 01:17:04,707
ACTUALLY, I HAVEN'T REALLY
EVEN MADE UP MY MIND YET,

1341
01:17:04,837 --> 01:17:06,056
SO IF EVERYBODY
COULD JUST--

1342
01:17:06,186 --> 01:17:09,189
OH, HONEY.

1343
01:17:09,320 --> 01:17:10,974
GIVE ME A HUG.

1344
01:17:13,803 --> 01:17:16,283
SWEETIE, YOU NEVER KNOW
WHAT'S GONNA HAPPEN.

1345
01:17:16,414 --> 01:17:20,505
OKAY? FOR A WHILE THERE,
I THOUGHT I'D NEVER GET MARRIED.

1346
01:17:20,636 --> 01:17:22,376
FINALLY, I HAD
TO PUT MY FOOT DOWN,

1347
01:17:22,507 --> 01:17:24,988
OR MY GUY HERE
WOULD NEVER HAVE LEFT--

1348
01:17:26,859 --> 01:17:28,818
[ phone rings ]

1349
01:17:31,821 --> 01:17:33,039
[ rings ]

1350
01:17:33,170 --> 01:17:34,345
I'LL GET THAT.

1351
01:17:39,350 --> 01:17:40,351
HELLO?

1352
01:17:42,745 --> 01:17:46,400
HONEY, IT'S THEIR MOTHER
CALLING FROM VIRGINIA.

1353
01:17:46,531 --> 01:17:48,707
IT SEEMS YOUR GRANDMOTHER
HAD A BAD FALL.

1354
01:17:48,838 --> 01:17:50,840
YOUR MOTHER WANTS YOU
TO MEET HER THERE.

1355
01:17:55,366 --> 01:17:57,760
DO YOU THINK
SHE'S OKAY IN THERE?

1356
01:17:57,890 --> 01:17:59,892
IT HAS BEEN A WHILE.

1357
01:18:00,023 --> 01:18:02,765
[ yells ]
GRANDMA, ARE YOU ALL...RIGHT?

1358
01:18:02,895 --> 01:18:07,595
YES, I'M JUST SMOKING
A LITTLE MARIJUANA.

1359
01:18:09,815 --> 01:18:12,775
LOOK AT THAT PATTERN.

1360
01:18:12,905 --> 01:18:14,385
IS IT JUST ME,

1361
01:18:14,515 --> 01:18:17,997
OR IS THAT THE SPITTIN' IMAGE
OF ABRAHAM LINCOLN?

1362
01:18:18,128 --> 01:18:21,522
LOOK, HALLEY, LOOK.
SEE, THERE'S THE MOLE.

1363
01:18:22,959 --> 01:18:24,830
HALLEY, YOU MUST SEE IT!

1364
01:18:24,961 --> 01:18:27,528
YOU'RE THE ONE WHO SEES THINGS
NO ONE ELSE CAN SEE.

1365
01:18:27,659 --> 01:18:28,486
I DO?

1366
01:18:28,616 --> 01:18:29,922
YES.

1367
01:18:30,053 --> 01:18:31,707
YOU'RE NOT SUPPOSED
TO BE WALKING YET.

1368
01:18:31,837 --> 01:18:33,926
NEXT TIME YOU FALL LIKE THAT,
YOU'RE GONNA BREAK YOUR HIP.

1369
01:18:34,057 --> 01:18:35,580
THEN YOU'RE GOING TO DIE.

1370
01:18:37,408 --> 01:18:38,452
HALLEY...

1371
01:18:39,540 --> 01:18:40,846
YOU REMEMBER
WHEN WE WENT

1372
01:18:40,977 --> 01:18:42,892
TO SEE OUR COMET
TOGETHER?

1373
01:18:43,022 --> 01:18:44,415
MM-HM.

1374
01:18:44,545 --> 01:18:46,156
Lydia: HALLEY WAS TOO YOUNG
TO REMEMBER THAT.

1375
01:18:46,286 --> 01:18:47,505
NO, I DO REMEMBER.

1376
01:18:47,635 --> 01:18:48,767
YOU CAN'T POSSIBLY.

1377
01:18:48,898 --> 01:18:50,203
YOU REMEMBER
HEARING ABOUT IT AFTER.

1378
01:18:50,334 --> 01:18:51,683
NO, MOM, I DO REMEMBER.

1379
01:18:51,814 --> 01:18:54,773
WHY DOES NO ONE TRUST ME
TO KNOW WHAT I KNOW ANYMORE?

1380
01:18:54,904 --> 01:18:56,209
GOD.

1381
01:18:58,603 --> 01:18:59,604
GOD!

1382
01:19:09,657 --> 01:19:10,789
SHE DOESN'T EVEN THINK

1383
01:19:10,920 --> 01:19:13,270
THAT MY OWN MEMORIES
BELONG TO ME.

1384
01:19:17,404 --> 01:19:19,189
DARLING,
SHE'S YOUR MOTHER.

1385
01:19:27,066 --> 01:19:31,375
NOW, TELL ME ABOUT
THIS FELLA OF YOURS.

1386
01:19:31,505 --> 01:19:33,769
WHO TOLD YOU ABOUT THAT?

1387
01:19:35,858 --> 01:19:39,470
GRANDMA, IT'S REALLY OVER.

1388
01:19:40,950 --> 01:19:44,780
FIRST LOVES ARE NEVER
REALLY OVER.

1389
01:19:47,913 --> 01:19:50,089
NOBODY'S PERFECT,
SWEETHEART.

1390
01:19:50,220 --> 01:19:53,484
BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN
IT WASN'T WORTH YOUR WHILE.

1391
01:19:56,835 --> 01:19:59,795
OH, BOY! DO I HAVE
THE MUNCHIES!

1392
01:20:06,410 --> 01:20:07,541
WHAT ABOUT HIM?

1393
01:20:07,672 --> 01:20:09,326
HE'S NOT
TERRIBLE-LOOKING.

1394
01:20:09,456 --> 01:20:10,806
YEAH, HE'S EVEN CUTE

1395
01:20:10,936 --> 01:20:13,896
IN THAT GEEKY WAY
YOU LIKE GUYS, ASHLEY.

1396
01:20:14,026 --> 01:20:15,506
HALLEY, IT'S...

1397
01:20:16,899 --> 01:20:18,683
IT'S LEWIS.

1398
01:20:47,277 --> 01:20:50,106
ASHLEY, LOVE OF MY LIFE...

1399
01:20:50,236 --> 01:20:53,239
LIFE OF MY HEART...

1400
01:20:53,370 --> 01:20:55,372
ONCE AGAIN...

1401
01:20:55,502 --> 01:20:56,852
WILL YOU MARRY ME?

1402
01:21:03,510 --> 01:21:05,077
YES.

1403
01:21:05,208 --> 01:21:06,122
YES.

1404
01:21:06,252 --> 01:21:07,950
YES. HOW CRAZY.

1405
01:21:08,080 --> 01:21:10,082
HOW CRAZY.
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

1406
01:21:16,959 --> 01:21:18,090
DO IT.

1407
01:21:32,583 --> 01:21:34,063
I OWE YOU ONE.

1408
01:21:35,978 --> 01:21:37,457
FOR?

1409
01:21:37,588 --> 01:21:39,982
MACON'S A REALLY GREAT GUY.

1410
01:21:40,112 --> 01:21:41,244
SEE YA, HALLEY.

1411
01:21:53,430 --> 01:21:54,431
HALLEY.

1412
01:21:55,954 --> 01:21:57,173
HEY.

1413
01:21:57,303 --> 01:21:58,696
HI.

1414
01:22:03,440 --> 01:22:06,312
I HAD NO IDEA
YOU GUYS WERE LIKE...

1415
01:22:06,443 --> 01:22:07,835
HANGING OUT.

1416
01:22:09,011 --> 01:22:10,403
ELIZABETH GUNDERSON AND ME?

1417
01:22:10,534 --> 01:22:11,448
NO, WE'RE JUST--

1418
01:22:11,578 --> 01:22:12,449
FRIENDS?

1419
01:22:12,579 --> 01:22:13,580
YEAH.

1420
01:22:14,581 --> 01:22:15,626
RIGHT.

1421
01:22:17,149 --> 01:22:19,717
NO, IT'S FINE,
BECAUSE WE HAD OUR THING,

1422
01:22:19,847 --> 01:22:21,110
AND IT WAS FUN...

1423
01:22:21,240 --> 01:22:23,025
UNTIL IT WASN'T ANYMORE,
RIGHT?

1424
01:22:23,155 --> 01:22:24,765
NO, THAT'S NOT IT.

1425
01:22:24,896 --> 01:22:27,029
WHEN THE GOING GETS TOUGH,
IT'S BEST TO JUST KEEP GOING,

1426
01:22:27,159 --> 01:22:28,639
DON'T YOU THINK?

1427
01:22:30,510 --> 01:22:32,991
COME ON, WOULD YOU LISTEN
TO ME FOR A SEC?

1428
01:22:43,175 --> 01:22:44,916
AND TO MY BRIDE.

1429
01:22:45,047 --> 01:22:46,222
THANK YOU FOR SHOWING ME

1430
01:22:46,352 --> 01:22:49,138
THAT SOCKS DON'T NEED
TO BE IRONED,

1431
01:22:49,268 --> 01:22:52,010
THAT ONE NEEDN'T EMPLOY
THE DEWEY DECIMAL SYSTEM

1432
01:22:52,141 --> 01:22:54,491
FOR THEIR CD COLLECTION,

1433
01:22:54,621 --> 01:22:55,971
AND THAT, IN THE END,

1434
01:22:56,101 --> 01:22:57,885
IT REALLY DOESN'T MAKE
A WHOLE LOT OF DIFFERENCE

1435
01:22:58,016 --> 01:22:59,452
WHETHER YOU START
THE TOILET PAPER

1436
01:22:59,583 --> 01:23:01,759
FACING UP OR DOWN...

1437
01:23:01,889 --> 01:23:04,196
DESPITE--DESPITE WHAT
MY PARENTS TAUGHT ME.

1438
01:23:06,198 --> 01:23:08,331
BECAUSE, ASHLEY,
YOU HAVE SHOWN ME

1439
01:23:08,461 --> 01:23:10,811
THAT LIFE
IS WORTH EMBRACING.

1440
01:23:10,942 --> 01:23:13,945
EVEN IF IT MEANS MAKING
A GIANT FOOL OF YOURSELF.

1441
01:23:14,076 --> 01:23:15,729
AND LUCKY FOR ME,

1442
01:23:15,860 --> 01:23:17,079
YOU'RE WILLING
TO MARRY THE GUY

1443
01:23:17,209 --> 01:23:19,211
WHO'S BEEN
THE BIGGEST FOOL OF ALL.

1444
01:23:19,342 --> 01:23:23,868
SO HERE'S TO A LIFETIME
OF BIG, MESSY,

1445
01:23:23,999 --> 01:23:25,870
WONDERFULLY
OUT-OF-ORDER MOMENTS

1446
01:23:26,001 --> 01:23:28,525
WITH THE MOST BEAUTIFUL WOMAN
IN THE WORLD--

1447
01:23:28,655 --> 01:23:30,179
MY BRIDE.

1448
01:23:31,702 --> 01:23:33,008
OH...

1449
01:24:14,614 --> 01:24:18,053
YOUR BIG SISTER IS
GETTING MARRIED IN 3 1/2 HOURS.

1450
01:24:21,882 --> 01:24:23,319
BUT YOU KNOW
IF YOU GET NERVOUS,

1451
01:24:23,449 --> 01:24:24,798
YOU CAN ALWAYS...

1452
01:24:26,496 --> 01:24:27,975
YOU REMEMBER THE SIGN.

1453
01:24:28,106 --> 01:24:30,848
OF COURSE. YOU TAUGHT IT
TO ME, REMEMBER?

1454
01:24:30,978 --> 01:24:32,632
SO, YOU KNOW. JUST...

1455
01:24:33,981 --> 01:24:35,331
LIKE THAT.
UH-HUH.

1456
01:24:35,461 --> 01:24:37,768
I'LL DO SOMETHING.
I'LL YELL, "FIRE!" OKAY?

1457
01:24:37,898 --> 01:24:38,769
OKAY.

1458
01:24:38,899 --> 01:24:39,944
OKAY.

1459
01:24:44,818 --> 01:24:47,517
AND WE'RE BACK
WITH THE BIG DOG OF SOFT ROCK.

1460
01:24:47,647 --> 01:24:50,694
WDYG, 94 FM.
"WE DIG THE DOG."

1461
01:24:50,824 --> 01:24:53,088
AND THIS IS DADDY DOG HIMSELF,
LEN MARTIN,

1462
01:24:53,218 --> 01:24:55,786
COMING TO YOU TODAY
ON A VERY SPECIAL DAY,

1463
01:24:55,916 --> 01:24:58,397
'CAUSE ONE OF MY
VERY OWN PUPPIES, THE ELDEST,

1464
01:24:58,528 --> 01:25:00,182
ASHLEY, IS GETTING MARRIED.

1465
01:25:00,312 --> 01:25:02,880
LORNA, HONEY,
ANY WORDS OF WISDOM

1466
01:25:03,010 --> 01:25:03,968
COMING FROM YOU,

1467
01:25:04,099 --> 01:25:05,317
MY VERY OWN NEWLYWED?

1468
01:25:05,448 --> 01:25:06,579
UH-HUH.

1469
01:25:06,710 --> 01:25:07,624
WATERPROOF MASCARA.

1470
01:25:07,754 --> 01:25:09,278
Len: I'M GONNA BORROW YOURS,

1471
01:25:09,408 --> 01:25:11,062
'CAUSE DADDY IS
GONNA BE WEEPING LIKE A BABY.

1472
01:25:11,193 --> 01:25:14,196
ALL RIGHT, LET'S KICK OFF
THIS POWER HOUR OF LOVE.

1473
01:25:14,326 --> 01:25:15,240
HALLEY?

1474
01:25:15,371 --> 01:25:16,459
HALLEY,

1475
01:25:16,589 --> 01:25:18,025
ARE YOU OUT THERE? SECURITY!

1476
01:25:18,156 --> 01:25:20,637
HEY, GIVE ME--COME ON.
THIS IS MY JOB!

1477
01:25:23,509 --> 01:25:24,945
MY HALLEY?

1478
01:25:25,076 --> 01:25:27,426
I DON'T KNOW HOW TO GET YOU
TO LISTEN, BUT--

1479
01:25:27,557 --> 01:25:28,949
Lorna: LEN, LET HIM TALK.

1480
01:25:29,080 --> 01:25:31,038
JUST HEAR ME OUT.

1481
01:25:31,169 --> 01:25:33,084
UM...

1482
01:25:33,215 --> 01:25:36,261
I SUCK WITH WORDS.

1483
01:25:36,392 --> 01:25:39,046
BUT SOMETIMES,
WORDS AREN'T THE THING.

1484
01:25:39,177 --> 01:25:41,614
LOVE ISN'T ABOUT WORDS,
IT'S ABOUT WHAT YOU DO.

1485
01:25:41,745 --> 01:25:43,964
AND WHAT I DID...

1486
01:25:44,095 --> 01:25:47,403
RUNNING AWAY,
IT WAS STUPID.

1487
01:25:47,533 --> 01:25:51,320
WE BOTH KNOW LOVE'S
A BIG, SCARY, EVIL CONCEPT.

1488
01:25:51,450 --> 01:25:53,017
BUT IF YOU FEEL IT,

1489
01:25:53,148 --> 01:25:54,888
IT'S GONNA FOLLOW YOU AROUND
LIKE A HUNGRY DOG

1490
01:25:55,019 --> 01:25:56,455
NO MATTER HOW FAR YOU RUN.

1491
01:25:56,586 --> 01:25:58,979
WAIT. I DIDN'T MEAN
TO SAY LOVE'S A DOG,

1492
01:25:59,110 --> 01:26:00,764
I JUST MEAN...

1493
01:26:00,894 --> 01:26:02,983
I'M NOT GOING ANYWHERE.

1494
01:26:03,114 --> 01:26:05,464
I LOVE YOU, HALLEY.

1495
01:26:05,595 --> 01:26:06,726
IF LOVE BEATS US UP,

1496
01:26:06,857 --> 01:26:08,380
LET'S JUST BEAT IT UP
RIGHT BACK.

1497
01:26:08,511 --> 01:26:10,077
WE COULD DO THIS, HALLEY.

1498
01:26:10,208 --> 01:26:11,905
IF YOU'RE READY
TO MAKE THE JUMP,

1499
01:26:12,036 --> 01:26:14,038
I'LL BE RIGHT HERE
TO CATCH YOU.

1500
01:26:21,001 --> 01:26:22,351
AND WHAT A POWERFUL

1501
01:26:22,481 --> 01:26:25,397
POWER HOUR OF LOVE
IT HAS BEEN.

1502
01:26:25,528 --> 01:26:28,574
THIS IS LEN MARTIN
FOR WDYG,

1503
01:26:28,705 --> 01:26:30,663
THE BIG DOG
OF SOFT ROCK.

1504
01:26:30,794 --> 01:26:32,404
THAT'S RIGHT--
ROMANCE IS IN THE AIR.

1505
01:26:32,535 --> 01:26:34,363
IT'S EVERYWHERE
HERE TODAY, FOLKS.

1506
01:26:34,493 --> 01:26:37,670
AND THIS NEXT SONG IS GOING OUT
TO THAT YOUNG LADY IN QUESTION,

1507
01:26:37,801 --> 01:26:40,630
MISS HALLEY MARTIN
AND HER BIG SISTER ASHLEY,

1508
01:26:40,760 --> 01:26:42,588
'CAUSE DADDY LOVES YOU.

1509
01:26:42,719 --> 01:26:46,113
[ Wild World
by Cat Stevens plays ]

